{id="t0222-01",kind="set",pieces={"Thread","FirstAidKit"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Spool of thread and first-aid kit",body="The thread spool and first-aid kit have the same black paint. A fresh scrape shows an older evacuation color underneath.",anchor={print="HouseforSale930"}},
-- T0223
{id="t0223-01",kind="set",pieces={"SeedBag","Notebook"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Seed bag and notebook",body="A seed bag is stored with the house plan and a notebook. A note asks the inspector to keep the garden dry till field visit.",anchor={print="HouseforSale929"}},
-- T0224
{id="t0224-01",kind="set",pieces={"Needle","Clipboard"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Sewing needle and clipboard",body="Road dust coats the needle and clipboard, but the ties look newly cut. The roll of names was neatly trimmed off the clipboard. I think the bundle was repacked after travel.",anchor={print="HouseforSale919"}},
-- T0225
{id="t0225-01",kind="set",pieces={"Notebook","Pencil"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Notebook and pencil",body="The notebook lists crop rotation schedules for every field. But pencil marks reserve one plot for a program test. That runs past the harvest date.",anchor={print="LeafhillHeights"}},
-- T0226
{id="t0226-01",kind="set",pieces={"SeedBag","Pistol"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Seed bag and pistol",body="Checkpoint tag 14 is tied to the seed bag and the pistol. The order on it says to say nothing about either. The evacuation list beside it has every name crossed off.",anchor={print="FarmingAndRuralSupplyDoeValley"}},
-- T0227
{id="t0227-01",kind="set",pieces={"Yarn","HandTorch"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Ball of yarn and torch",body="The yarn and torch are wedged beneath unused warning tape. Footprints pass around the bundle rather than toward it.",anchor={print="LennysCarRepair"}},
-- T0228
{id="t0228-01",kind="set",pieces={"Notebook","Pencil"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Notebook and pencil",body="The notebook marks evacuation complete. The pencil tally ends halfway down the page. The rest is blank.",anchor={print="CarFixation"}},
-- T0229
{id="t0229-01",kind="set",pieces={"Screwdriver","PetrolCan"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Screwdriver and petrol can",body="The screwdriver's here, work half-done. Petrol can's empty. They fueled up and left for the fields anyway.",anchor={print="AlsAutoShop"}},
-- T0230
{id="t0230-01",kind="set",pieces={"Hammer","Nails"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Hammer and nails",body="Brand new hammer and a box of nails, still in the checkout area. Someone was supposed to pick these up before they shut down. Guess the evacuation didn't go as smoothly as they said.",anchor={print="NailsAndNuts"}},
-- T0232
{id="t0232-01",kind="set",pieces={"Hammer","Nails"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Hammer and nails",body="These nails and hammer were marked field-use before they shipped. Part of the program deployment, the tag says. Why rush tools to empty fields?",anchor={print="WPDIY"}},
-- T0233
{id="t0233-01",kind="set",pieces={"LeatherStrips","BathTowel"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Leather strips and towel",body="Four notches on the leather strips match four marks on the towel. A fifth mark was sanded flat on both.",anchor={print="EPToolsLV"}},
-- T0234
{id="t0234-01",kind="set",pieces={"Notebook","WaterBottle"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="notebook and water bottle",body="Notebook shows spray schedule got mixed up last week. Same fields got hit twice, maybe three times. Water bottle has that chemical smell the crops had.",anchor={print="RosewoodFD"}},
-- T0235
{id="t0235-01",kind="set",pieces={"Broom","Fertilizer"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Broom and fertilizer sack",body="The broom and fertilizer sack share a sweet pesticide smell. Dead moths are stuck only where the two touched.",anchor={print="BrandenburgFD"}},
-- T0236
{id="t0236-01",kind="set",pieces={"Gloves_LeatherGloves","Notebook"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Leather gloves and notebook",body="The notebook logs visitors until noon. The final entry says the briefing continues. The leather gloves were never signed back in.",anchor={print="LVFD"}},
-- T0237
{id="t0237-01",kind="set",pieces={"Notebook","Pencil"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="notebook and pencil",body="Spray schedules fill the notebook pages. The pencil circled overlapping dates. Same plots got treated multiple times.",anchor={print="MuldraughPD"}},
-- T0238
{id="t0238-01",kind="set",pieces={"Pills","Notebook"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Pills and notebook",body="Notebook has a quarantine stamp over the attendance roster. Pills inside match orders to distribute at evacuation checkpoints. Two names logged but their dose is still here untouched.",anchor={print="LVPDHQ"}},
-- T0239
{id="t0239-01",kind="set",pieces={"Pistol","SheetPaper2"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Pistol and sheet of paper",body="The pistol lies on the paper. It lists checkpoint duty, ticked complete before inspection. Someone wrote 'how many through?' at the bottom, blank.",anchor={print="RiversidePD"}},
-- T0240
{id="t0240-01",kind="set",pieces={"Soap2","Briefcase"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Soap and briefcase",body="found the briefcase beneath a table at the Riverside checkpoint, warning tape across it. two bars of soap inside marked decontamination issue, and a status sheet listing six evacuees. four are checked through, two crossed out in red. at the bottom it says file restricted, but the whole station got abandoned.",anchor={print="HouseforSale845"}},
-- T0241
{id="t0241-01",kind="set",pieces={"SeedBag","WaterBottle"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Seed bag and water bottle",body="A garden seed packet is stored with a water bottle. A property note says the next owner should wait for a soil test.",anchor={print="HouseforSale851"}},
-- T0242
{id="t0242-01",kind="set",pieces={"Sponge","Map"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Sponge and map",body="Opposite route arrows are painted on the sponge and road map. The older arrow was scraped away under fresh road grit.",anchor={print="HouseforSale855"}},
-- T0243
{id="t0243-01",kind="set",pieces={"WaterBottle","Notebook"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Water bottle and notebook",body="The notebook shows a water test form and a signed rental agreement. Someone noted the upstream fields were sprayed tuesday. The bottle smells sweet when I open it.",anchor={print="HouseforSale860"}},
-- T0244
{id="t0244-01",kind="set",pieces={"ToiletPaper","WalkieTalkie1"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Toilet paper and radio",body="The toilet roll and radio are sealed together, never opened. Soot darkens the bundle. Clean outlines look like it was packed before the fire.",anchor={print="PremisesforLease863"}},
-- T0245
{id="t0245-01",kind="set",pieces={"Tissue","FirstAidKit"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Tissues and first-aid kit",body="Pale spray residue streaks one face of the tissues and first-aid kit. Field dust is on the other face. Field twine is knotted at the handle with a few seed husks.",anchor={print="HouseforSale867"}},
-- T0246
{id="t0246-01",kind="set",pieces={"FishingRod","HandTorch"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Fishing rod and torch",body="A fishing rod and hand torch by the dock, both left behind. The torch was still on when I got here this morning. They cleared out before the roadblock went up at dawn.",anchor={print="CabinforRentDixie"}},
-- T0247
{id="t0247-01",kind="set",pieces={"Candle","AnimalFeedBag"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Candle and feed bag",body="The animal feed bag reeks of chemicals I can't name. Pellets inside have an oily green coating. A candle sits melted on top. Batch numbers and test dates run along the seam.",anchor={print="WPTownHall"}},
-- T0248
{id="t0248-01",kind="set",pieces={"Bread","Map"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Bread and map",body="The bread's clipped to the map. Stamped before they closed the depot, left the last groups stranded.",anchor={print="DinerInTheWoods"}},
-- T0249
{id="t0249-01",kind="set",pieces={"Book","LetterHandwritten"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Book and handwritten letter",body="A handwritten letter is tucked in a book. It says to cover the well after they sprayed the nearby fields. The water went cloudy and all the crops wilted.",anchor={print="FallasLakeChurch"}},
-- T0250
{id="t0250-01",kind="set",pieces={"Book","SheetPaper2"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Book and sheet of paper",body="Containment order on the paper. The book says assess the threat first. They didn't wait.",anchor={print="OldCGECorpBuilding"}},
-- T0251
{id="t0251-01",kind="set",pieces={"RadioBlack","SheetPaper2"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Radio and sheet of paper",body="The band schedule lists an extra set after closing. A venue note asks staff to air out the room after the field crew. Their boots tracked in spray-wet soil with a sweet chemical smell.",anchor={print="RustyRifle"}},
-- T0252
{id="t0252-01",kind="set",pieces={"SeedBag","WaterBottle"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="seed bag and water bottle",body="Guard tag 22 hangs on the seed bag and the water bottle. Tape across both says nobody moves them until the convoy comes. The checkpoint count on the tag reads six people.",anchor={print="A1Hay"}},
-- T0253
{id="t0253-01",kind="set",pieces={"Matches","HandTorch"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Matches and torch",body="Red and blue cord join the box of matches to the torch. The red route is cut. The blue route ends in a sealed knot.",anchor={print="Airport"}},
-- T0254
{id="t0254-01",kind="set",pieces={"Screwdriver","SheetPaper2"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Screwdriver and sheet of paper",body="The paper says the containment checks are complete. The screwdriver's still in its wrapper. Nobody opened anything to inspect.",anchor={print="AMZSteel"}},
-- T0255
{id="t0255-01",kind="set",pieces={"Bread","Bag_ALICEpack"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Bread and pack",body="The bread and pack came with a note listing trial rows to spray. A receipt shows the delivery was paid before the crew left.",anchor={print="BeefChunk"}},
-- T0256
{id="t0256-01",kind="set",pieces={"Lighter","GardeningSprayEmpty"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="lighter and spray bottle",body="Checkpoint tape binds the lighter and the empty spray bottle. Patrol tag 7 says two people, do not enter. A note orders everyone to stay silent.",anchor={print="BrottAuction"}},
-- T0257
{id="t0257-01",kind="set",pieces={"FishFillet","KitchenKnife"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Fish fillet and kitchen knife",body="The fish fillet is cut halfway through. Kitchen knife set down beside it. The meat has an oily film that smells like chemicals.",anchor={print="CatonaHotTinGrill"}},
-- T0258
{id="t0258-01",kind="set",pieces={"Extinguisher","Camera"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Fire extinguisher and camera",body="The extinguisher and camera are wrapped in a child's raincoat. They're sealed with barrier tape and a cordon sticker over the seal. The sticker has an inked number, and a struck-through one under it.",anchor={print="Coalfield"}},
-- T0259
{id="t0259-01",kind="set",pieces={"HandTorch","Notebook"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Torch and notebook",body="The notebook logged checkpoint evacuations. Last headcount reads blank, pages after torn away. The hand torch lies on it, lens covered in barrier tape.",anchor={print="ColdWarBunker"}},
-- T0260
{id="t0260-01",kind="set",pieces={"AlcoholWipes","Briefcase"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Alcohol wipes and briefcase",body="A broken barrier board crushed the wipes against the briefcase. The clean undersides show both were there before the road was blocked.",anchor={print="DarkwallowGuestHouse"}},
-- T0261
{id="t0261-01",kind="set",pieces={"Book","Notebook"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Book and notebook",body="The book's about field trial procedures. The notebook ends in june. Someone shut down the program before collecting the final data.",anchor={print="EkronCollege"}},
-- T0262
{id="t0262-01",kind="set",pieces={"EmptyJar","Pencil"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Empty jar and pencil",body="The jar's empty. A pencil was left here with supply tallies. The marks stop mid-week, shifts still unfed.",anchor={print="FiveAlarmChili"}},
-- T0263
{id="t0263-01",kind="set",pieces={"Bandage","Notebook"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Bandage and notebook",body="The notebook's care log lists a routine delivery. The field sample box was marked outside before the resident came. A bandage lay on top of it.",anchor={print="GoldenSunset"}},
-- T0264
{id="t0264-01",kind="set",pieces={"Pistol","Pistol2"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Two pistols",body="Two pistols tagged for issue. The ammo count was never done. Transfer dated the day the containment zone went up.",anchor={print="GunsUnlimitedEchoCreek"}},
-- T0265
{id="t0265-01",kind="set",pieces={"Hammer","Nails"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Hammer and nails",body="Found a hammer and nails by the fence. Repairs were on hold for a soil test. Those trial rows yellowed right after the spray.",anchor={print="HobbsandPerkinsHardware"}},
-- T0266
{id="t0266-01",kind="set",pieces={"Antibiotics","Map"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Antibiotics and map",body="Three pickup dots mark the antibiotics and road map. Two were scratched away with no wear around them.",anchor={print="HouseforSale787"}},
-- T0267
{id="t0267-01",kind="set",pieces={"WaterBottle","Notebook"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Water bottle and notebook",body="The listing packet has a water test booked after the move-in date. A note asks the owner to leave the kitchen tap unused. The well sits beside a sprayed field and the water has run cloudy.",anchor={print="HouseforSale799"}},
-- T0268
{id="t0268-01",kind="set",pieces={"AnimalFeedBag","WalkieTalkie1"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Feed sack and radio",body="The feed sack is tied to the radio by a clipped lanyard. It carries a roadblock pass with the headcount blacked out. An empty loop shows a tag was cut off; barrier tape holds the dial.",anchor={print="HouseforSale818"}},
-- T0269
{id="t0269-01",kind="set",pieces={"Pistol","Notebook"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Pistol and notebook",body="I found a notebook tracking spray schedules and sick crop rows. The damage spread faster each week they kept spraying. A pistol lay beside it.",anchor={print="IrvingtonGunClub"}},
-- T0270
{id="t0270-01",kind="set",pieces={"Scissors","SheetPaper2"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Scissors and sheet of paper",body="The paper shows evacuation routes, parts snipped with scissors. Marked finished, but whoever approved it left no signature. No name on the order.",anchor={print="LoveDuet"}},
-- T0271
{id="t0271-01",kind="set",pieces={"Calculator","FirstAidKit"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Calculator and first-aid kit",body="The calculator and first-aid kit have the same black paint. A fresh scrape shows an older evacuation color underneath.",anchor={print="MadDansDen"}},
-- T0273
{id="t0273-01",kind="set",pieces={"VHS_Retail","SheetPaper2"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Video tape and sheet of paper",body="The sheet of paper marks evacuation complete. The video tape shows roads jammed, people still fleeing. Someone signed it off early.",anchor={print="MusicFest93"}},
-- T0274
{id="t0274-01",kind="set",pieces={"Notebook","WaterBottle"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Notebook and water bottle",body="The notebook's farm delivery card lists a water sample with the eggs. The water bottle is dated after the cartons were collected.",anchor={print="OvoFarms"}},
-- T0275
{id="t0275-01",kind="set",pieces={"SeedBag","Pizza"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Seed bag and pizza",body="The guards left a seed bag and a pizza box at the checkpoint. A wall list orders everyone to wait here for transport. Roadblock tape still closes the road.",anchor={print="Pondview"}},
-- T0276
{id="t0276-01",kind="set",pieces={"MeasuringTape","GardeningSprayEmpty"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Measuring tape and garden sprayer",body="The tape and empty garden sprayer share a sticky pale-blue residue. I think it's from the same spray run. A few seed husks are stuck in the tape's housing.",anchor={print="QuillManor"}},
-- T0277
{id="t0277-01",kind="set",pieces={"Comb","HandTorch"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Comb and torch",body="The comb and torch are wedged beneath unused warning tape. Footprints pass around the bundle rather than toward it.",anchor={print="Sammies"}},
-- T0278
{id="t0278-01",kind="set",pieces={"HandTorch","Map"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Torch and map",body="The tour map marks the basement route open. Barrier tape is across the route, with a number penciled by each step. They count down to a closed door, torch lens taped to a slit.",anchor={print="Sanatorium"}},
-- T0279
{id="t0279-01",kind="set",pieces={"Toothbrush","BathTowel"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Toothbrush and towel",body="Four notches on the toothbrush match four marks on the towel. A fifth mark was sanded flat on both.",anchor={print="SleepEazzzeInn"}},
-- T0280
{id="t0280-01",kind="set",pieces={"Screwdriver","SheetPaper2"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Screwdriver and paper",body="The paper shows the sprayer was set to triple concentration.\nI found the screwdriver next to the valve adjustment notes.\nSomeone ran the test without resetting it.",anchor={print="StuartandLogScrapyard"}},
-- T0281
{id="t0281-01",kind="set",pieces={"Book","Map"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Book and map",body="The store map is folded into a book with a handwritten translation. The log says the room was empty before the last visitor signed out.",anchor={print="TheWizardsKeep"}},
-- T0282
{id="t0282-01",kind="set",pieces={"WaterBottle","SheetPaper2"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Water bottle and sheet of paper",body="The sheet lists application dates for crop treatments. Someone checked off the final round before the first. The water bottle still has dilution marks on the side.",anchor={print="Twiggys"}},
-- T0283
{id="t0283-01",kind="set",pieces={"HandShovel","Bucket"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Hand shovel and bucket",body="Feed sack marking from the treated rows streaks the shovel and bucket. Dead flies fill the bottom ring of the bucket. The shovel blade has a bitter green film.",anchor={scene="RBBar"}},
{id="t0283-02",kind="set",pieces={"GlassTumbler","DishCloth"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="glass tumbler and dish cloth",body="The glass has tape marked evacuation zone specimen. The cloth is stiff with dried bleach. I think they cleaned the counter before taking the glass.",anchor={scene="RBBar"}},
-- T0284
{id="t0284-01",kind="written",pieces={"notepad"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Notepad page",body="My note from dusk: the trial crew left their rinsed gloves on the fence rail after spraying the far rows. My brother started coughing as the wind turned toward the barn.\n\nI wrote it down while I still remembered which rows got the new mix. The smell stayed in the barn all night. I put this page apart from the ordinary feed tallies.",anchor={scene="RBBarn"}},
{id="t0284-02",kind="written",pieces={"notepad"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Notepad page",body="I told them the barn was empty after the morning count. It was true if you counted people. The two calves were still there, and I could hear the smaller one pressing its head against the gate whenever a truck stopped outside.\n\nA man in a vest asked for the ledger, then wrote the barn down as cleared on the evacuation list and told me not to say otherwise. He took the kitchen calendar too. By evening the gate had a new chain. Nobody asked me to feed them, and nobody said I could go back in.\n\nI left the milk pail by the door because I thought a person who came to lock it would see it. In the morning the pail was gone. The list on the post still said cleared.",anchor={scene="RBBarn"}},
-- T0285
{id="t0285-01",kind="set",pieces={"FirstAidKit","WaterBottle"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="First-aid kit and water bottle",body="Clouded residue from the treated rows streaks the kit and bottle. It was set aside after the flies vanished from the barn. The cattle began to cough.",anchor={scene="RBBurnt"}},
{id="t0285-02",kind="set",pieces={"FirstAidKit","WaterBottle"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="First-aid kit and water bottle",body="The kit is unopened, with a stenciled cordon number on the lid. The bottle has a black line halfway down, repeated on the burnt wall. Looks like measuring what survived the fire, not treating a burn.",anchor={scene="RBBurnt"}},
-- T0286
{id="t0286-01",kind="written",pieces={"letter"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="corpse",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Letter",body="I kept the sealed seed packet you asked about. The trial crew sprayed the near rows around midnight; by morning the leaves had curled and my brother started coughing.\n\nWe needed the supplies listed here for the following morning. The crew left their empty sacks behind and never said what was in the mix.\n\nI do not know the name of it. The older packet is the one I had in my hands that day.",anchor={scene="RBBurntCorpse"}},
{id="t0286-02",kind="written",pieces={"letter"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="corpse",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Letter",body="If they ask you who started it, tell them I went inside for the dog. I did. I also went back for the camera from the shelf, the silver one.\n\nThe men outside told me to leave it where it was. One held the door while the other watched me search. When I came out without it, they let me sit by the truck. They were careful with me then. They had already put the camera in a bag of their own.\n\nThe dog came out through the back, singed and furious. Please give her water first. I don't want her remembered as another thing I left inside.",anchor={scene="RBBurntCorpse"}},
-- T0287
{id="t0287-01",kind="set",pieces={"Potato","EmptyJar"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="corpse",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Potato and empty jar",body="The potato and jar sit beside a marked feed sack. Field dust lies beneath them. Sticky spray residue and seed husks cling to the bundle.",anchor={scene="RBBurntFireman"}},
{id="t0287-02",kind="set",pieces={"Potato","EmptyJar"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="corpse",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Potato and empty jar",body="Scratched on the jar's bottom: 447. Inked on the potato: 531. One family's stock, two different evacuation codes.",anchor={scene="RBBurntFireman"}},
-- T0288
{id="t0288-01",kind="written",pieces={"diary"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Diary page",body="Before breakfast: the crop trial crew brought rinsed gloves. my brother started coughing. I washed everything twice, but the sweet smell of the spray stayed in the sink.\n\nI used the margin to note what we actually found: curled leaves, dead bees.\n\nI wrote the names of the trial rows in the space left for expenses.",anchor={scene="RBCafe"}},
{id="t0288-02",kind="written",pieces={"diary"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Diary page",body="The woman at the next table asked why they were taking names with the breakfast order. I told her it was probably for the bill. The waitress folded the list and put it in her apron, though we had all paid at the counter.\n\nLater a man in a gray protective suit came in through the kitchen, spoke to her, and left with the folded paper. Nobody cleared our plates while he was there. I kept looking at the clock because my sister was due to meet me.\n\nShe never arrived. I wrote down the time, then crossed it out when I realized I couldn't remember whether the clock had stopped before or after the man came in. The waitress set a fresh pot on the stove and kept serving everyone else.",anchor={scene="RBCafe"}},
-- T0289
{id="t0289-01",kind="set",pieces={"Battery","RadioBlack"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="battery and radio black",body="The battery and radio black were under the tarp when they sprayed. Corn burned yellow the next morning. I found dead crows in every furrow.",anchor={scene="RBClinic"}},
{id="t0289-02",kind="set",pieces={"Battery","RadioBlack"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Battery and radio",body="The battery is taped into the radio with a strip of medicine label. The dial is fixed in place. Looks like the clinic kept one frequency ready after broadcasts ended.",anchor={scene="RBClinic"}},
-- T0290
{id="t0290-01",kind="written",pieces={"notepad"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Notepad page",body="The trial crew sprayed the rows behind the house before dawn. My brother started coughing an hour later. I found their empty drum by the fence. The leaves there had curled by sunrise.",anchor={scene="RBDorm"}},
{id="t0290-02",kind="written",pieces={"notepad"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Notepad page",body="Room count at noon: four beds slept in, six beds assigned, eight names on the door. Nobody could explain the difference. We had made the list from the doors because the office list had been taken.\n\nA visitor came back with the office list in her hand and asked us to erase two names. She did not ask whether either student was still here. We argued about it quietly because the girl in the end bed was asleep.\n\nBy supper the visitor had gone. I wrote the two names again on a scrap and pushed it into my shoe. If somebody asks tomorrow, I can say I made a mistake. I would rather have a mistake I can show them.",anchor={scene="RBDorm"}},
-- T0291
{id="t0291-01",kind="set",pieces={"FishingRod","WaterBottle"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Fishing rod and water bottle",body="The rod and bottle both smell like the creek below the test fields. I think someone dropped them when the headaches started. That was before they drained the whole reservoir.",anchor={scene="RBGunstoreSiege"}},
{id="t0291-02",kind="set",pieces={"Battery","RadioBlack"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Battery and radio",body="A battery sits by a radio with no tuning knob. It looks like the barricade could hear only one station. I think nobody inside could change it.",anchor={scene="RBGunstoreSiege"}},
-- T0292
{id="t0292-01",kind="written",pieces={"diary"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Diary page",body="Three customers from the east fields brought the same sweet chemical smell in their hair. They said the crop trial crew had sprayed the rows before sunrise. I washed everyone twice and the smell stayed in the towels.\n\nThe next week their hands were raw, and the sprayed rows had gone yellow in strips. I wrote it down here so I would remember which field they named.",anchor={scene="RBHairSalon"}},
{id="t0292-02",kind="written",pieces={"notepad"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Notepad page",body="I kept the book open so they could see when the last customer had come in. The woman asked for the names instead of the times.\n\nShe did not take the whole book. She tore out two pages and left the small notes about hair color and the money owed. One customer had asked me to call his wife. I still have her number, but I cannot remember which page it was on.\n\nWe swept after they left. A curl of paper caught under the chair and I put it here in case the customer comes back to pay.",anchor={scene="RBHairSalon"}},
-- T0293
{id="t0293-01",kind="set",pieces={"Axe","SeedBag"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="vehicle",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Axe and seed bag",body="An axe and a seed bag are bundled beside a clouded sample jar. Field dust lies under them, and road tape is caught around the bundle.",anchor={scene="RBHeatBreakAfternoon"}},
{id="t0293-02",kind="set",pieces={"Map","WaterBottle"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="vehicle",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Map and water bottle",body="The map is folded to hide three streets. The bottle has a fresh mark for each one. I think whoever drove here was counting stops early.",anchor={scene="RBHeatBreakAfternoon"}},
-- T0294
{id="t0294-01",kind="written",pieces={"diary"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Field notebook page",body="The trial supervisor left application instructions on the porch. My brother mixed the concentrate without gloves that afternoon. By evening his hands were blistered and he couldn't stop shaking. I saved the instruction sheet when we left the house.",anchor={scene="RBJoanHartford"}},
{id="t0294-02",kind="written",pieces={"letter"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Handwritten letter",body="They told us the list was for families. I believed them until the families arrived and nobody would let them see it.\n\nOne woman recognized a coat through the window. The man at the door said the coat belonged to a different person and closed the curtain. She waited for hours because no one would tell her whose coat she had seen.\n\nI wrote down the time they took the list. If she comes back I can at least tell her when we stopped being allowed to answer.",anchor={scene="RBJoanHartford"}},
-- T0295
{id="t0295-01",kind="set",pieces={"Mop","Bucket"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Mop and bucket",body="Both still have the amber residue from those trial plots. I remember the mop handle smelled sweet before people got sick. The bucket sat outside the clinic once they banned further use.",anchor={scene="RBJudge"}},
{id="t0295-02",kind="set",pieces={"Notebook","Pencil"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Notebook and pencil",body="The notebook has two dates written over each other. The pencil points to the earlier entry. The margin says the hearing was closed before anyone arrived.",anchor={scene="RBJudge"}},
-- T0296
{id="t0296-01",kind="written",pieces={"notepad"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Notepad page",body="My note from near midnight: the field trial crew carried rinsed gloves home from the rows. My brother started coughing after he handled them, and the lettuce in the yard curled by morning.\n\nI folded the corner so I could find the entry again. I left this one unfolded for whoever came after us.",anchor={scene="RBLooted"}},
{id="t0296-02",kind="written",pieces={"diary"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Diary page",body="They came while the room was still full. I thought they were stopping the stealing, but one of them knew which drawer held the names.\n\nI stood outside with a neighbor who was holding a lamp. We heard drawers open, then the men carried out one thin folder. They left the money and the jewelry where the thieves had scattered it.\n\nIn the morning the front door was broken and everyone said the folder had been stolen with the rest. I could not persuade the neighbor to say what we had seen.",anchor={scene="RBLooted"}},
-- T0297
{id="t0297-01",kind="set",pieces={"WalkieTalkie1","FirstAidKit"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Walkie talkie and first aid kit",body="The walkie talkie and first aid kit are soaked in pesticide. I found them where the spray crew worked that morning. Everyone got sick hours after the fields were treated.",anchor={scene="RBMayorWestPoint"}},
{id="t0297-02",kind="set",pieces={"Newspaper","Pencil"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Newspaper and pencil",body="A newspaper and a pencil lie here. Someone penciled earlier times over the evacuation schedule. Makes it look like warnings went out sooner than they did.",anchor={scene="RBMayorWestPoint"}},
-- T0298
{id="t0298-01",kind="written",pieces={"letter"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Handwritten letter",body="I kept the sealed seed packet you asked about. The trial crew passed before breakfast and my brother started coughing after he handled it. The seedlings in the bed beside it came up white and then fell over.\n\nI had promised to bring this home for supper. Its date and the empty chair at the table now belong to the same evening.",anchor={scene="RBNolans"}},
{id="t0298-02",kind="written",pieces={"letter"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Handwritten letter",body="The first man said they were checking on us. The second asked which neighbors had left and wrote their names before he asked whether they were well.\n\nI told them the little boy next door was with his aunt. He had gone to fetch her because she was alone. When the men returned, they asked me to say that both houses had been empty since noon.\n\nI can say I misunderstood the hour. I cannot explain why they came back to change it.",anchor={scene="RBNolans"}},
-- T0299
{id="t0299-01",kind="set",pieces={"Bread","CannedCorn"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Bread and canned corn",body="Bread and canned corn are bundled beside a marked feed sack. Field dust lies under them and has worked into the coat hem.",anchor={scene="RBOffice"}},
{id="t0299-02",kind="set",pieces={"Sheet","Pencil"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Sheet of paper and pencil",body="Someone used the pencil to change the count on the sheet. I can still see the original number beneath the marks. The new one is lower.",anchor={scene="RBOffice"}},
-- T0300
{id="t0300-01",kind="written",pieces={"diary"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Diary page",body="Before dawn: the crop trial crew brought rinsed gloves back from the rows. My brother started coughing. I washed everything twice and the water ran cloudy and sweet-smelling.\n\nThe beans along the fence turned black at the edges the same week. I meant to ask the crew about the spray in the morning.",anchor={scene="RBOther"}},
{id="t0300-02",kind="written",pieces={"notepad"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Notepad page",body="He wanted the room cleared before he opened his bag. We moved the chairs into the hall and he put three envelopes on the table.\n\nThe first was for the people still here. The other two had names of places already shut. He took those away when I asked him why he had come so late.\n\nI thought he would leave a copy. Instead he asked for the empty envelopes back, too. The chairs are still in the hall because no one knows whether the room is open.",anchor={scene="RBOther"}},
-- T0301
{id="t0301-01",kind="set",pieces={"KeyRing","GardeningSprayEmpty"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Key ring and empty sprayer",body="The key ring and empty sprayer are streaked from a clouded sample jar. Sprayer residue has dried hard on both. I think they were put aside once the flies left the field edge.",anchor={scene="RBPileOCrepe"}},
{id="t0301-02",kind="written",pieces={"letter"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Handwritten letter",body="I was told to leave the kitchen open for one more shift, though the road count already included its address. I set aside a clean apron for the morning cook.\n\nThe second list, the one for people waiting inside, came back with no names. The man who carried it said the count was final and I was not to correct it.",anchor={scene="RBPileOCrepe"}},
-- T0302
{id="t0302-01",kind="written",pieces={"notepad"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Notepad page",body="My note from near lunchtime: a sprayer was left running at the shop door and the delivery bags on the shelf were dusted yellow. The whole place smelled of feed and weedkiller.\n\nI did not know where to put the bags once the shelves were wiped. I could not mistake the sick seedlings in the window for anything but spray damage.",anchor={scene="RBPizzaWhirled"}},
{id="t0302-02",kind="written",pieces={"notepad"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Notepad page",body="At closing I counted the remaining boxes and wrote the number on the lid. A driver came for them after I had put away the register.\n\nHe had a list of shelter addresses, but it was folded so I could only see the first. He crossed it out without unloading anything, and told me the number I had written was to be changed to zero. I was to say nothing about the shipment if asked, and the access road was to stay closed.",anchor={scene="RBPizzaWhirled"}},
-- T0303
{id="t0303-01",kind="set",pieces={"HandShovel","Bucket"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Hand shovel and bucket",body="A hand shovel rests across a bucket, both striped with yellow dust. The bucket smells of crop spray. Road tape is knotted through its handle.",anchor={scene="RBPoliceSiege"}},
{id="t0303-02",kind="set",pieces={"Battery","RadioBlack"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Battery and radio",body="The radio dial is bound with a narrow strip of tape. The battery looks recently replaced. I can't tell how anyone barricaded here could reply.",anchor={scene="RBPoliceSiege"}},
-- T0304
{id="t0304-01",kind="written",pieces={"notepad"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Notepad page",body="In the margin I wrote what the farmers said at the door: the corn was curling after the spray and the cattle would not eat the new feed. Some thought the mix had been too strong.\n\nWe tried to finish the ordinary work around it. The leaves by the side door were still yellow at dark.",anchor={scene="RBReverend"}},
{id="t0304-02",kind="written",pieces={"notebook"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Notebook page",body="I was asked to read the list aloud and I did. One name was missing, though the person was sitting right there. I thought the page had been copied badly.\n\nAfterward the visitor asked me not to add the name. She said another office had already settled it. The person stayed to help stack the chairs and asked why everyone had begun speaking softly.\n\nI wrote the name in the margin of my own book. It is not a record anyone will accept, but I could not bring myself to leave an empty space.",anchor={scene="RBReverend"}},
-- T0305
{id="t0305-01",kind="set",pieces={"FirstAidKit","SeedBag"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="First aid kit and seed bag",body="A first aid kit sits open beside a split seed sack. Yellow dust covers the gauze. Black road tape is stuck to the sack.",anchor={scene="RBSWATStation"}},
{id="t0305-02",kind="set",pieces={"Battery","RadioBlack"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Battery and radio",body="The battery looks new, and the radio is wrapped in a shirt. Tape holds the dial on the channel used before the order to leave.",anchor={scene="RBSWATStation"}},
-- T0306
{id="t0306-01",kind="written",pieces={"diary"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Diary page",body="Thursday: spray residue was on the spare room window and the potted tomatoes had yellowed overnight. The dog would not touch its feed.\n\nI wrote down the name on the drum by the fence. I wondered what else got sprayed up the road.",anchor={scene="RBSafehouse"}},
{id="t0306-02",kind="written",pieces={"diary"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Diary page",body="They gave us a count for the beds and told us it was final. Then another family arrived at the back door with a child too tired to stand.\n\nWe made room and I put her shoes under the bed so nobody would trip. In the morning the list still had the old count. A visitor looked at the shoes and asked us to move them before the next inspection.\n\nThe child did not understand why her mother kept calling her by a different name. I did, but I did not tell her.",anchor={scene="RBSafehouse"}},
-- T0307
{id="t0307-01",kind="set",pieces={"WaterBottle","EmptyJar"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="water bottle and empty jar",body="I find a water bottle and empty jar bound with twine. Pale spray residue lines the inside of both. The jar's label mentions crop treatment concentrate.",anchor={scene="RBSchool"}},
{id="t0307-02",kind="set",pieces={"Book","Pencil"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Book and pencil",body="The roll book is open to an ordinary lesson. A pencil note on the back looks like a later head count. It includes pupils missing from the official list.",anchor={scene="RBSchool"}},
-- T0308
{id="t0308-01",kind="written",pieces={"receipt"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Paper receipt",body="Soap, gloves, and two water jugs, paid cash. On the back: \"Bought spray for the north field and the seed corn came up curled. The cattle will not touch the new feed.\"\n\nI saved it from the bag of rubbish because the note named the spray. The things stacked beside the page were real enough, and still dusted yellow.",anchor={scene="RBShopLooted"}},
{id="t0308-02",kind="written",pieces={"notepad"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Notepad page",body="The shelves were emptied twice. The first group took what was on them; the second stepped over the broken glass to ask for the ledger.\n\nI showed them the register—the ledger was gone. They wanted the names from that morning. When they found one woman and her son, they wrote those down, asked when I'd last seen them, if they'd said where they were going. The tape went across the door when they left. They told me not to mention their visit and took the register with them.",anchor={scene="RBShopLooted"}},
-- T0309
{id="t0309-01",kind="set",pieces={"Mop","Bucket"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="mop and bucket",body="A mop sits in a bucket of yellow chemical film. The smell is sharp, almost sweet. Bootprints lead in from the crop sprayer outside.",anchor={scene="RBSpiffo"}},
{id="t0309-02",kind="set",pieces={"DishCloth","Paperclip"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Dish cloth and paperclip",body="A dish cloth by a paperclip, bent open now. It held papers once, I think. They wiped clean and took only what was clipped here.",anchor={scene="RBSpiffo"}},
-- T0310
{id="t0310-01",kind="written",pieces={"photograph"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Photo with writing",body="Written on it: the application crew left yellow residue everywhere. We felt dizzy for hours and the potted plants all wilted.\n\nI found it filed with the other trial documents.",anchor={scene="RBStripclub"}},
{id="t0310-02",kind="written",pieces={"letter"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Handwritten letter",body="I wrote the closing time on the chalkboard. Later a man asked me to rub it out and say we had shut earlier.\n\nThe people at the last table were still here when he came in. One of them had gone to call a friend and left a coat behind. I did not know whether to give the coat back when the man took their names.\n\nThe board is clean. The coat is in the cupboard with my own things. If anyone comes for it, I will tell them when I last saw its owner.",anchor={scene="RBStripclub"}},
-- T0311
{id="t0311-01",kind="set",pieces={"Bread","FirstAidKit"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="bread and first aid kit",body="The loaf has green spray grit on its crust. The first aid kit smells of weedkiller. Both were tied with twine near a wilted crop row.",anchor={scene="RBTSBreakfast"}},
{id="t0311-02",kind="set",pieces={"Bowl","Spoon"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Bowl and spoon",body="The bowl has scratches inside, grouped in fives like a count. The spoon tip is worn sharp from marking. More marks than the posted number outside.",anchor={scene="RBTSBreakfast"}},
-- T0312
{id="t0312-01",kind="written",pieces={"notebook"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Notebook page",body="I wrote down when the spray rig ran behind the shop and which rows it covered. The meat was still cold, but the flies were dying at the vents.\n\nI wrote the time and the field on a page before I went back for the others. The clock may have been slow; the yellow residue was on the back door by evening.",anchor={scene="RBTSButcher"}},
{id="t0312-02",kind="written",pieces={"notepad"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Notepad page",body="The shopkeeper made me bring the parcel through the back. He said the front counter was closed to anyone who had been beyond the roadblock.\n\nA visitor checked the wrapper but never asked what was inside. He took the slip with the customer name and told us both that the parcel was not to be handed out or discussed, and that the name would be kept on his list. He left the parcel on the table.",anchor={scene="RBTSButcher"}},
-- T0314
{id="t0314-01",kind="set",pieces={"Potato","EmptyJar"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="potato and empty jar",body="A potato cut in half and an empty jar both carry gray waxy residue. The jar smells like the fertilizer concentrate it once held.",anchor={scene="RBTSDinner"}},
{id="t0314-02",kind="set",pieces={"Spoon","Bowl"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Spoon and bowl",body="A spoon lies across evacuation papers with crossed-out counts. The bowl has a tag number absent from the official ledger.",anchor={scene="RBTSDinner"}},
-- T0315
{id="t0315-01",kind="written",pieces={"letter"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Handwritten letter",body="I saved the bottle for you because it smelled like the trial orchard after spraying. I poured out the glasses before anyone drank, and the rinse water left a film on the sink.\n\nThe leaves on the pear tree outside the window had curled the same week. I could not mistake the empty place left for the person we had been waiting for.",anchor={scene="RBTSDrink"}},
{id="t0315-02",kind="written",pieces={"letter"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Handwritten letter",body="I put aside four glasses after the men came in. They said the others would be back for them and asked me to write the names on a napkin.\n\nI watched them pour the drinks away when they thought I had gone. They kept the napkin, and one of them told me the names were not to be repeated to anyone, including the four.",anchor={scene="RBTSDrink"}},
-- T0316
{id="t0316-01",kind="set",pieces={"Battery","RadioBlack"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Battery and black radio",body="A fresh battery is taped to a black radio. Green spray flecks cover the antenna and fill the speaker grille. The dial is set to an agricultural channel.",anchor={scene="RBTSElectronics"}},
{id="t0316-02",kind="set",pieces={"RadioBlack","Battery"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Radio and battery",body="A radio sits beside a loose battery. A pencil mark on the dial matches one on the workbench. Every other frequency is scratched away. Tape over the dial shows only a time.",anchor={scene="RBTSElectronics"}},
-- T0317
{id="t0317-01",kind="written",pieces={"notepad"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Notepad page",body="My note says the farm crew washed their sample jars in this sink. The water turned milky and left a grey film on the pans. By morning the herbs in the window had gone limp and my tongue felt numb.\n\nI left this page where the next person would look.",anchor={scene="RBTSFoodPreparation"}},
{id="t0317-02",kind="written",pieces={"notepad"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Duty log",body="The last shift was marked complete but no one signed out. I found their gear still in the lockers. Someone wrote 'relocated' next to each name. The supervisor's notes for that day are torn out.",anchor={scene="RBTSFoodPreparation"}},
-- T0318
{id="t0318-01",kind="set",pieces={"CannedCorn","Bandage"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Canned corn and bandage",body="A can of corn and a bandage are wrapped in evidence tape. Both are stamped cleared for distribution. The blood under the tape dried days before the stamp.",anchor={scene="RBTSSandwich"}},
{id="t0318-02",kind="set",pieces={"Spoon","Paperclip"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Spoon and paperclip",body="I found a spoon and a paperclip stuck in a feed sack lining the tray. The lot mark doesn't match the mixing ratio scrawled next to it.",anchor={scene="RBTSSandwich"}},
-- T0319
{id="t0319-01",kind="written",pieces={"diary"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Diary page",body="Friday: I mended three work shirts from the seed trial. White powder shook from every cuff and my hands blistered by evening. The thread I used went brittle in a day.\n\nI kept the stained shirt rather than a cleaned one, because the powder showed which field the crew had worked.",anchor={scene="RBTSSewing"}},
{id="t0319-02",kind="written",pieces={"diary"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Diary page",body="The woman brought in a coat with its pocket torn. While I pinned it, a folded list fell out. She asked me to sew the pocket closed with the list inside.\n\nShe said her brother would need the coat if he returned, and that nobody official was to see the list. I used a different color along the seam so the paper could be found without ruining the whole coat.",anchor={scene="RBTSSewing"}},
-- T0320
{id="t0320-01",kind="set",pieces={"WaterBottle","TinOpener"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Water bottle and tin opener",body="Chicken feed dust coats the inside of the water bottle. Dried crop spray crusts the tin opener's handle. Both smell like the sick corn rows.",anchor={scene="RBTSSoup"}},
{id="t0320-02",kind="set",pieces={"Bowl","Spoon"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Bowl and spoon",body="Twenty-three scratches inside the bowl. The spoon shows nineteen notches, one crossed out. Both were carried to the table and left.",anchor={scene="RBTSSoup"}},
-- T0321
{id="t0321-01",kind="set",pieces={"Saw","Plank"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Saw and plank",body="Someone left this saw and plank ready for a repair. No record of what needed fixing, no orders I can find. They were prepared before anyone admitted there was a problem.",anchor={scene="RBTrashed"}},
{id="t0321-02",kind="set",pieces={"Bucket","HandShovel"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Bucket and hand shovel",body="A bucket has a faded field lot mark under a newer cleaning label. The hand shovel has the same fine yellow dust caught in its handle.",anchor={scene="RBTrashed"}},
-- T0322
{id="t0322-01",kind="written",pieces={"letter"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Handwritten letter",body="I saved the cloth with a sweet chemical smell for you. The field trial crew passed Thursday after closing and the rats left the shed. By morning the garden beds beside the shed had turned white and slick.\n\nThe mark did not come off when I tried to wash my hands.",anchor={scene="RBTwiggy"}},
{id="t0322-02",kind="written",pieces={"notepad"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Notepad page",body="A man sat by the back door and asked for the names of everyone who had come in. I assumed he meant the people still here.\n\nHe wanted the earlier customers too. I wrote down the one I knew because she brought her own mug. He crossed out her name, then asked whether I was certain she had arrived.\n\nHer mug is still under the counter. I have not washed it, though I cannot say what that proves.",anchor={scene="RBTwiggy"}},
-- T0323
{id="t0323-01",kind="set",pieces={"KeyRing","Bucket"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="key ring and bucket",body="A key ring and a bucket share a bitter residue. The sprayer went over the same field twice that morning. Nobody expected the dosage to stack like that.",anchor={scene="RBWoodcraft"}},
{id="t0323-02",kind="written",pieces={"notepad"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Notepad page",body="The men building shelves were told to make another partition before the evacuation trucks came. Someone measured for beds and then scratched the measurements out. My brother still brought his tools, because the invoice for the first day had already been paid.",anchor={scene="RBWoodcraft"}},
-- T0324
{id="t0324-01",kind="written",pieces={"diary"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="spray log page",body="the dilution was mixed wrong on the second batch. workers near the treated rows started smelling like harsh solvent.\n\nthe hens by the irrigation line went completely still. I saw foam pooling where the chemical runoff collected.\n\nI wrote this after the third time I noticed the same pattern.",anchor={scene="RDSBandPractice"}},
{id="t0324-02",kind="written",pieces={"notepad"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Notepad page",body="We were halfway through the same song for the third time when a visitor came in and asked us to lower the volume. He needed to hear the radio in the hallway.\n\nThe voice on it was reading street names. One of us lived on the first street and went to call home. The visitor shut the door before the next name.\n\nWe tried to play again. Nobody could remember the first line, so I wrote the streets down instead.",anchor={scene="RDSBandPractice"}},
-- T0325
{id="t0325-01",kind="set",pieces={"FirstAidKit","WaterBottle"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="corpse",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="First aid kit and water bottle",body="A first aid kit and water bottle are tied together. Blue powder coats one side and has caked into the bottle's threads. A few shriveled seedlings are stuck in it.",anchor={scene="RDSBanditRaid"}},
{id="t0325-02",kind="set",pieces={"Map","Pencil"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="corpse",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Map and pencil",body="A map and a pencil are kept together in a pocket. Three homes are circled, but only one is crossed off. I think the mark was made before the door was forced.",anchor={scene="RDSBanditRaid"}},
-- T0326
{id="t0326-01",kind="written",pieces={"notepad"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Notepad page",body="Personal note: wash off the white crystals left by the livestock-feed study crew. The creek smelled wrong and the cattle at the fence would not drink from it.\n\nI folded the corner so I could find the entry again. I kept the page because it was the only one with our address.",anchor={scene="RDSBathroomZed"}},
{id="t0326-02",kind="written",pieces={"letter"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Handwritten letter",body="I heard someone knock while I was hiding here. He said he was checking the rooms and read a list aloud.\n\nThe name of the person with me was on it, though she had not told anyone we were here. She whispered that they had copied an older list from another building.\n\nHe left after we stayed quiet. I wrote the names I could remember so I can ask her later where that list came from.",anchor={scene="RDSBathroomZed"}},
-- T0327
{id="t0327-01",kind="set",pieces={"Potato","EmptyJar"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Potato and empty jar",body="A cut potato and a sample jar share red grit from the fertilizer test. They were bundled before the buses quit running.",anchor={scene="RDSBedroomZed"}},
{id="t0327-02",kind="set",pieces={"WaterBottle","Bandage"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Water bottle and bandage",body="A bottle of water and a strip of bandage have matching pencil marks. They look like dates, not doses. I think someone checked this bed before its occupant woke.",anchor={scene="RDSBedroomZed"}},
-- T0328
{id="t0328-01",kind="written",pieces={"letter"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="corpse",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Handwritten letter",body="I saved the cloth with sticky pollen for you. The orchard spray test crew passed the late afternoon; the mare refused her feed, and afterward the bridge was blocked.\n\nI had promised to bring this home for supper. Its date and the empty chair at the table now belong to the same evening.\n\nI could have mistaken the order in which those things happened. I could not mistake the empty place left for the person we had been waiting for.",anchor={scene="RDSBleach"}},
{id="t0328-02",kind="written",pieces={"letter"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="corpse",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Handwritten letter",body="I asked for clean water. The man with the bucket asked how many people were still here before he opened it.\n\nI pointed to the room behind me. He wrote down a smaller number and said the others would be counted separately. He would not say where.\n\nThe bucket was emptied on the floor after he left. I kept the scrap he dropped because it has the number he first wrote.",anchor={scene="RDSBleach"}},
-- T0329
{id="t0329-01",kind="set",pieces={"Mop","Bucket"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="corpse",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Mop and bucket",body="A mop and a rinse bucket share black specks from the pasture study. They were bundled after the grass behind them got the same specks.",anchor={scene="RDSCorpsePsycho"}},
{id="t0329-02",kind="set",pieces={"Pencil","Sheet"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="corpse",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Pencil and sheet of paper",body="A pencil and a torn sheet are folded together in a pocket. The sheet lists rooms by number. The last two are struck out in a different hand.",anchor={scene="RDSCorpsePsycho"}},
-- T0330
{id="t0330-01",kind="written",pieces={"diary"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Diary page",body="Monday morning: two workers from the seed trial carried an oily film on their boots. My eyes began burning, and the sprouts in the tray they walked past slumped overnight.\n\nI meant to ask about it in the morning. This page is what I have of the answer.",anchor={scene="RDSDeadDrunk"}},
{id="t0330-02",kind="written",pieces={"diary"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Diary page",body="We thought he had fallen asleep and left him on the couch. A man at the door asked us to write down when we had last spoken to him.\n\nHe wanted one time for all of us. We disagreed because some of us had left the room. He wrote down his own time and asked us to sign below it.\n\nI still have the bottle cap he put beside the paper to hold it flat. I do not know whose account that paper is supposed to be.",anchor={scene="RDSDeadDrunk"}},
-- T0331
{id="t0331-01",kind="set",pieces={"Battery","RadioBlack"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="corpse",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="battery and black radio",body="A battery and black radio lie caked in dried green pesticide. Crop chaff clogs the speaker grille. The antenna is thick with chemical spray.",anchor={scene="RDSDevouredByRats"}},
{id="t0331-02",kind="set",pieces={"Paperclip","Pencil"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="corpse",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Paperclip and pencil",body="This pencil eraser is worn to bare metal. The paperclip held something thick, now missing. They cleared everything else when they evacuated.",anchor={scene="RDSDevouredByRats"}},
-- T0332
{id="t0332-01",kind="written",pieces={"notepad"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Notepad page",body="Personal note: wash off the gray foam left by the feed additive trial crew. My brother started coughing, and the hens would not touch the feed from that sack.\n\nI did not know where to put the sack after the shelves were cleared. I put the note under it.",anchor={scene="RDSFootballNight"}},
{id="t0332-02",kind="written",pieces={"notepad"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Notepad page",body="At halftime we heard the street announcement through the open window. The others kept watching the game and I wrote the names of the roads on the back of the score sheet.\n\nSomeone came by after dark and asked me for it. He already knew the score and said he only wanted to check my spelling.\n\nI gave him the front half. The names are still here because I tore the page across the fold first.",anchor={scene="RDSFootballNight"}},
-- T0333
{id="t0333-01",kind="set",pieces={"Axe","SeedBag"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Hand axe and seed sack",body="Milky water from the water-treatment trial is on the axe and sack. The seed has sprouted pale, then rotted where the water touched.",anchor={scene="RDSGrouchos"}},
{id="t0333-02",kind="set",pieces={"DishCloth","WaterBottle"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Dish cloth and water bottle",body="A dish cloth is knotted around a water bottle. Inside is a penciled count of people seen that afternoon. One line looks altered after the cloth was washed.",anchor={scene="RDSGrouchos"}},
-- T0334
{id="t0334-01",kind="written",pieces={"letter"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="corpse",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Handwritten letter",body="I saved the cloth with yellow dust for you. The field-sprayer test crew passed Friday before dawn and three people felt dizzy. The corn leaves on the near rows were scorched by noon.\n\nWe tried to finish the ordinary work around it. The dust left yellow handprints on everything.",anchor={scene="RDSGunmanInBathroom"}},
{id="t0334-02",kind="written",pieces={"notepad"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="corpse",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Notepad page",body="He told us to stay in the room and wait for the count. We could hear boots in the hall and someone asking whether to include the people behind the bathroom door.\n\nThe answer was no. They read out a number, then asked us to leave one at a time. He stayed behind with the door locked.\n\nI wrote the number down because it was smaller than the number of voices I had heard.",anchor={scene="RDSGunmanInBathroom"}},
-- T0335
{id="t0335-01",kind="set",pieces={"Bread","CannedCorn"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="corpse",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Bread and canned corn",body="The loaf and canned corn smell sweet and chemical, like the crop plot. I think they were bundled before the lane was closed.",anchor={scene="RDSGunslinger"}},
{id="t0335-02",kind="set",pieces={"Map","DuctTape"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="corpse",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Map and duct tape",body="The map has an evacuation route erased in pencil. Duct tape on the back hides the first exit they marked. The printed path was changed.",anchor={scene="RDSGunslinger"}},
-- T0336
{id="t0336-01",kind="written",pieces={"diary"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Diary entry",body="Sunday after supper: two workers from the greenhouse trial carried a bitter residue on their sleeves. My hands blistered, and the cucumbers in our own plot yellowed by the next afternoon.\n\nI kept a pinch of the residue in a folded page as proof of what it smelled like.",anchor={scene="RDSHenDo"}},
{id="t0336-02",kind="written",pieces={"letter"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Handwritten letter",body="We put the guests names on a sheet so we could keep the surprise. A stranger arrived with a copy that had two names removed.\n\nHe asked whether those two had already left. I said one was still upstairs, getting ready. He folded his copy and waited at the foot of the stairs.\n\nNobody wanted to spoil the party by arguing. I have kept our list because it is the only one with everyone on it.",anchor={scene="RDSHenDo"}},
-- T0337
{id="t0337-01",kind="set",pieces={"Fertilizer","GardeningSprayEmpty"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="corpse",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Fertilizer sack and empty sprayer",body="The fertilizer sack and empty sprayer are tied together. One side has a sharp solvent smell. A torn strip of road tape covers the other.",anchor={scene="RDSHockeyPsycho"}},
{id="t0337-02",kind="set",pieces={"Pencil","Paperclip"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="corpse",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Pencil and paperclip",body="The paperclip holds two pages together. Someone used the pencil to change a seven to a one. I count the scratch marks underneath.",anchor={scene="RDSHockeyPsycho"}},
-- T0338
{id="t0338-01",kind="written",pieces={"notepad"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Notepad page",body="Personal note: wash off the blue powder left by the fertilizer test crew. The dog refused its water and the clover at the edge of the lawn went grey.\n\nThere may be a simple reason for it. Nobody I asked could say what the powder was meant to do.",anchor={scene="RDSHouseParty"}},
{id="t0338-02",kind="written",pieces={"diary"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Diary entry",body="We wrote names on the wall when the guest book disappeared. It was a joke until a visitor asked us to paint over them.\n\nOne friend had gone for more drinks and was not there to object. By morning somebody had covered only his name. The rest remained visible through the paint.\n\nI took a photograph before anyone did the second coat. I cannot tell if he came back while we were asleep.",anchor={scene="RDSHouseParty"}},
-- T0339
{id="t0339-01",kind="set",pieces={"HandShovel","Bucket"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Hand shovel and bucket",body="White crystals from the orchard spray test coat the shovel and pail. I think they were bundled before the bridge was blocked.",anchor={scene="RDSPokerNight"}},
{id="t0339-02",kind="set",pieces={"Pencil","Book"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Pencil and book",body="A pencil lies across an open book. The evacuation list counts one more name than beds in this shelter. Someone rubbed the last entry nearly clean, I think.",anchor={scene="RDSPokerNight"}},
-- T0340
{id="t0340-01",kind="written",pieces={"letter"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="corpse",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Handwritten letter",body="I saved the cloth with red grit for you. The pasture study crew passed on the first hot day; the flies vanished and the grass behind them went rust-coloured in a ragged line.\n\nThe younger one wanted to throw it away. I put it where neither of us could forget.",anchor={scene="RDSPoliceAtHouse"}},
{id="t0340-02",kind="written",pieces={"letter"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="corpse",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Handwritten letter",body="They asked me to count the people inside while they were still walking through the house. I gave the number I knew.\n\nOne of them looked at a folded sheet and said it was too high. He asked whether a visitor had already gone home. The visitor was asleep upstairs.\n\nI left the number on the back of this envelope. If someone asks later, I want to remember what I actually saw.",anchor={scene="RDSPoliceAtHouse"}},
-- T0341
{id="t0341-01",kind="set",pieces={"FirstAidKit","WaterBottle"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="corpse",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="First-aid kit and water bottle",body="Sticky pollen from the seed trial is on the kit and the bottle. The inside of the bottle went slimy with the same pollen. I think they were bundled after that.",anchor={scene="RDSPrisonEscape"}},
{id="t0341-02",kind="set",pieces={"Map","Pencil"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="corpse",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Map and pencil",body="The pencil and map share the same pocket. A route toward the road is overwritten with a line back inside. That line is traced twice, like it was copied.",anchor={scene="RDSPrisonEscape"}},
-- T0342
{id="t0342-01",kind="written",pieces={"diary"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="corpse",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Diary entry",body="Tuesday at dusk: two workers from the pest-control test carried black specks on their clothes. The garden browned within the hour, and the bees by the hive lay in rows.\n\nI wrote this down while I could still remember which workers it was.",anchor={scene="RDSPrisonEscapeWithPolice"}},
{id="t0342-02",kind="written",pieces={"letter"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="corpse",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Handwritten letter",body="We reached the gate before dawn. A man with a list asked us to give our names one at a time.\n\nWhen my companion spoke, the man stopped writing and looked at the person beside him. They argued over which list to use. We could see the road was clear.\n\nThey let the others through. We were told to wait for a second count, and I wrote the first count here so it would not disappear.",anchor={scene="RDSPrisonEscapeWithPolice"}},
-- T0343
{id="t0343-01",kind="set",pieces={"KeyRing","EmptyJar"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Key ring and empty jar",body="The key ring's tied to the empty jar with wire. An amber residue lines the jar bottom. Both items feel oily, smell chemical.",anchor={scene="RDSRPGNight"}},
{id="t0343-02",kind="written",pieces={"letter"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Handwritten letter",body="We played until a man outside told us the road would be closed at dawn. He let the other car through and said the count had been made yesterday. I kept my score sheet; it is the only record that we were here.",anchor={scene="RDSRPGNight"}},
-- T0344
{id="t0344-01",kind="written",pieces={"notepad"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Notepad page",body="Personal note: wash off the green flecks left by the water-treatment trial crew. The rats left the shed and the herbs by the back step died in a day.\n\nThe first account was spoken quickly, as if there might be a bus to catch. I wrote it down before another person could replace it.",anchor={scene="RDSRatInfested"}},
{id="t0344-02",kind="written",pieces={"notepad"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Notepad page",body="I counted the traps because I thought that was why they came. The visitor asked instead which doors we had opened that morning.\n\nHe marked one room as empty before looking in it. When I asked him to check again, he said the number had already been sent.\n\nThe traps remain. The door he marked empty is shut now, and I do not want to be the person who opens it.",anchor={scene="RDSRatInfested"}},
-- T0345
{id="t0345-01",kind="set",pieces={"Mop","Bucket"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Mop and bucket",body="Gray foam from the field-sprayer test has dried on the mop and bucket. A few dead beetles lie in the bottom of the bucket. They are bundled together.",anchor={scene="RDSRatWar"}},
{id="t0345-02",kind="set",pieces={"WaterBottle","Pencil"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Water bottle and pencil",body="A bottle is tied to a pencil with string. The tally on the bottle differs from the number on the sheet.",anchor={scene="RDSRatWar"}},
-- T0346
{id="t0346-01",kind="written",pieces={"letter"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Handwritten letter",body="I saved the cloth with milky water for you. The crop plot crew sprayed the rows Saturday near lunch. By evening two hens lay still by the fence and the trough water had gone cloudy.",anchor={scene="RDSResourceGarage"}},
{id="t0346-02",kind="written",pieces={"notepad"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Notepad page",body="I told them which shelves had fuel and which held tools. They asked for the names of people who had filled containers the night before.\n\nI could remember the man who paid in coins because I had counted them twice. His number was already on their sheet. They did not ask me about the fuel after that.\n\nI put the coins away separately. The drawer still has the gap where the sheet had been kept.",anchor={scene="RDSResourceGarage"}},
-- T0347
{id="t0347-01",kind="set",pieces={"Battery","RadioBlack"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="corpse",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Battery and black radio",body="Yellow dust from the greenhouse trial is on the battery and radio. I think they were bundled before the phones went dead.",anchor={scene="RDSSkeletonPsycho"}},
{id="t0347-02",kind="set",pieces={"Map","Rope"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="corpse",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Map and rope",body="The map shows collection points but one sector is scribbled over. The rope has counting knots along it but several are cut away. The numbers they reported can't be right.",anchor={scene="RDSSkeletonPsycho"}},
-- T0348
{id="t0348-01",kind="written",pieces={"diary"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="corpse",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Diary entry",body="The night shift: two workers from the livestock-feed study carried a sweet chemical smell in on their boots.\n\nBy morning the creek below their plot smelled the same, and the minnows were floating.",anchor={scene="RDSSpecificProfession"}},
{id="t0348-02",kind="written",pieces={"letter"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="corpse",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Handwritten letter",body="The man writing the names asked what I did for a living. I told him, and he put down something else.\n\nHe said the form had no space for my work. I could see there was a space; it was already filled. The person beside me told me to let him finish.\n\nI wrote my own occupation here because I do not want the next person to think I lied about it.",anchor={scene="RDSSpecificProfession"}},
-- T0349
{id="t0349-01",kind="set",pieces={"Axe","SeedBag"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Hand axe and seed sack",body="The axe and seed sack are tied together. Bitter yellow residue coats the axe head and soaked the sack. The sack smells of treated seed.",anchor={scene="RDSStagDo"}},
{id="t0349-02",kind="set",pieces={"GlassTumbler","Pencil"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Glass tumbler and pencil",body="A sheet and pencil are tucked under an empty glass. The guest count was changed after the first toast. The marks around the glass look like it sat there all night.",anchor={scene="RDSStagDo"}},
-- T0350
{id="t0350-01",kind="written",pieces={"notepad"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Notepad page",body="Personal note, the late afternoon: wash off the sharp solvent smell left by the orchard spray test crew.\n\nThe mare refused her feed, and her coat is spotted where the mist drifted over the fence.",anchor={scene="RDSStudentNight"}},
{id="t0350-02",kind="written",pieces={"notepad"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Notepad page",body="We were supposed to be studying. When the lights failed, we counted everyone by calling out names across the room.\n\nA visitor came with a shorter list and said two people had gone home. One of them answered from the far corner. He crossed her name out anyway.\n\nShe wanted to leave then, but none of us knew whether the door was still open. I kept this page with her name on it.",anchor={scene="RDSStudentNight"}},
-- T0351
{id="t0351-01",kind="set",pieces={"Bread","CannedCorn"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="corpse",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Bread and canned corn",body="Blue powder from the pasture study dusts the loaf and the corn. The loaf's wrapper has gone stiff with it.",anchor={scene="RDSSuicidePact"}},
{id="t0351-02",kind="set",pieces={"Sheet","Pencil"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="corpse",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Paper sheet and pencil",body="A folded sheet and pencil are held beneath the same hand. Two names are boxed together. A third is pressed in hard enough to leave a mark without ink.",anchor={scene="RDSSuicidePact"}},
-- T0352
{id="t0352-01",kind="written",pieces={"letter"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Handwritten note",body="The spray from the crop dusters left a film on everything outside. I came inside after working the field and my skin started burning. The animals stopped eating and the chickens died within two days. Now my hands have the same dark marks the livestock had.",anchor={scene="RDSTinFoilHat"}},
{id="t0352-02",kind="written",pieces={"diary"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Diary entry",body="I made a hat to keep the rain off the radio. It looked ridiculous, so nobody noticed when I carried it from room to room.\n\nThe same street names came through three times. After the second reading a visitor told us the broadcast had never happened and asked for the radio.\n\nI took the battery out first. The station may be silent now, but I want to know what it says if it comes back.",anchor={scene="RDSTinFoilHat"}},
-- T0353
{id="t0353-01",kind="set",pieces={"Fertilizer","GardeningSprayEmpty"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Fertilizer sack and empty sprayer",body="Red grit from the pest test is on the fertilizer sack and sprayer. I think they were bundled before the checkpoint appeared.",anchor={scene="RDSZombieLockedBathroom"}},
{id="t0353-02",kind="set",pieces={"Pencil","Sheet"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Pencil and paper sheet",body="A pencil and sheet are pushed beneath the door together. The sheet has an earlier head count with a later number over it. I can't see any sign the door was opened.",anchor={scene="RDSZombieLockedBathroom"}},
-- T0355
{id="t0355-01",kind="written",pieces={"notebook"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="corpse",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Notebook page",body="My coat pocket entry says the well-water study workers brushed off silver specks from their sprayer.\n\nThe mice abandoned the bin that night, and the water in the trough wore a silver film by morning.",anchor={scene="RDSZombiesEating"}},
{id="t0355-02",kind="written",pieces={"letter"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="corpse",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Handwritten letter",body="I counted four names in the book they carried, but only three people lay here. The man with the book asked me not to look for the fourth.\n\nHe turned the page toward me to show that the missing person had already been accounted for. The writing was too small to read and he closed it before I could ask.\n\nI wrote the four names as well as I remember them. I may have misspelled one, but I know I heard it.",anchor={scene="RDSZombiesEating"}},
-- T0356
{id="t0356-01",kind="set",pieces={"Potato","EmptyJar"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="vehicle",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Potato and empty jar",body="A jar and potato bear torn evacuation supply tags. One tag has a sector code struck through and corrected. Both carry the same emergency authority stamp.",anchor={scene="RVSAmbulanceCrash"}},
{id="t0356-02",kind="written",pieces={"notepad"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="vehicle",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Notepad page",body="My sister came in from the treated rows with burning eyes and blistered hands. Her work clothes reeked of the spray. By evening three neighbors who never entered the field had the same burning eyes.",anchor={scene="RVSAmbulanceCrash"}},
-- T0357
{id="t0357-01",kind="written",pieces={"photograph"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="vehicle",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Annotated photograph",body="On the back: “late Wednesday, emerald flecks in the cab after the crop trial. the chickens stopped moving in the yard.”\n\nThe flecks were still on the seat the next morning.",anchor={scene="RVSAnimalTrailerOnRoad"}},
{id="t0357-02",kind="written",pieces={"notebook"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="vehicle",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Checkpoint notes",body="The officials at the gate were counting people in each vehicle. I heard them argue about whether to count heads or just cars. They each wrote down different numbers on their clipboards.",anchor={scene="RVSAnimalTrailerOnRoad"}},
-- T0358
{id="t0358-01",kind="set",pieces={"Mop","Bucket"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="vehicle",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Mop and bucket",body="Brown foam from the greenhouse test is on the stiff mop and bucket. I think they were packed before the telephone line died.",anchor={scene="RVSBanditRoad"}},
{id="t0358-02",kind="written",pieces={"letter"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="vehicle",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Handwritten letter",body="The men at the road took our spare fuel and said the next checkpoint would let us through. I wrote the amount on the back of the grocery slip. There was no checkpoint there, only the cars they had already turned around.",anchor={scene="RVSBanditRoad"}},
-- T0359
{id="t0359-01",kind="written",pieces={"receipt"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="ground",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Paper receipt",body="Feed, soap, and a clean jar, paid cash. My note below says chalky water came from the feed test.\n\nThe ditch smelled metallic, and the frogs were gone from it by noon.",anchor={scene="RVSBurntCar"}},
{id="t0359-02",kind="written",pieces={"notepad"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="ground",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Notepad page",body="The car burned after they copied its registration onto the clear list. I watched them carry a new list to the far side of the road. My father was told he had never arrived, although his name was on my first copy.",anchor={scene="RVSBurntCar"}},
-- T0360
{id="t0360-01",kind="set",pieces={"Battery","RadioBlack"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="vehicle",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Battery and black radio",body="Mustard-colored dust from the fertilizer trial is caked in the seams. It's on the battery and radio, like it was carried in from the rows.",anchor={scene="RVSCarCrash"}},
{id="t0360-02",kind="written",pieces={"notebook"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="vehicle",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Notebook page",body="The driver had been told the south road was open to families. Someone moved the barrier while we stopped for water. He went back to ask and was offered a different map with the old road drawn out of it.",anchor={scene="RVSCarCrash"}},
-- T0361
{id="t0361-01",kind="written",pieces={"notebook"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="vehicle",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Notebook page",body="My cab entry says the orchard treatment workers brushed off a cloying orchard smell.\n\nThe horse kicked away its feed, and the leaves along the fence line had curled.",anchor={scene="RVSCarCrashCorpse"}},
{id="t0361-02",kind="written",pieces={"letter"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="vehicle",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Handwritten letter",body="The person beside me waited in the car while I asked for help. A man in a vest said the crash happened outside the area they were collecting names from. I wrote ours down anyway, so somebody might look for both of us.",anchor={scene="RVSCarCrashCorpse"}},
-- T0362
{id="t0362-01",kind="set",pieces={"Axe","SeedBag"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="vehicle",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="axe and seed bag",body="I found an axe and seed bag wrapped in checkpoint tape. The tag shows one location crossed out, another written over it. Tape edges say something about relocating citizens and files.",anchor={scene="RVSCarCrashDeer"}},
{id="t0362-02",kind="written",pieces={"notepad"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="vehicle",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Notepad page",body="The deer came from a pasture that had been sprayed yesterday. Its mouth was wet with a bitter smell, and its legs shook. The driver said the creek near the rows smelled the same.",anchor={scene="RVSCarCrashDeer"}},
-- T0363
{id="t0363-01",kind="written",pieces={"photograph"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="vehicle",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Annotated photograph",body="On the back: “the first morning, a medicinal odor in the cab after the experimental seed run. my throat tightened. The seedlings along the verge had blackened.”",anchor={scene="RVSChangingTire"}},
{id="t0363-02",kind="written",pieces={"notebook"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="vehicle",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Notebook page",body="A worker drew a chalk circle around the stopped car and promised a tow after the next convoy. The convoy arrived, took everyone able to walk, and crossed our names off his pad. I stayed to finish the tire and found the pad discarded.",anchor={scene="RVSChangingTire"}},
-- T0364
{id="t0364-01",kind="set",pieces={"KeyRing","CannedCorn"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="vehicle",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Key ring and canned corn",body="Violet powder from the insecticide test coats the key ring and corn. There's a clean print where a glove held them.",anchor={scene="RVSConstructionSite"}},
{id="t0364-02",kind="set",pieces={"WalkieTalkie1","DuctTape","Battery"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="vehicle",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Walkie-talkie, tape and battery",body="A work radio has its dial taped down on one channel. Spare batteries sit beside it. Someone told the crew to listen only, days before the road closed.",anchor={scene="RVSConstructionSite"}},
-- T0365
{id="t0365-01",kind="written",pieces={"receipt"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="vehicle",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Paper receipt",body="Feed, soap, and a clean jar, paid cash. My note below says saltlike grains came from the livestock supplement test.\n\nMy sister coughed all night, and the calves would not drink.",anchor={scene="RVSCrashHorde"}},
{id="t0365-02",kind="written",pieces={"notepad"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="vehicle",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Notepad page",body="At the bend they made us wait for a lead car before letting anyone through. The lead car never returned. The man who kept the count quietly drew a line through everyone still waiting when the road filled up.",anchor={scene="RVSCrashHorde"}},
-- T0366
{id="t0366-01",kind="set",pieces={"Fertilizer","GardeningSprayEmpty"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="ground",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="fertilizer and empty sprayer",body="Rust-colored grit from the well study coats the fertilizer sack. The empty sprayer ran dry during the second application. The wheat in that plot turned black within a week.",anchor={scene="RVSDeadEnd"}},
{id="t0366-02",kind="written",pieces={"notebook"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="ground",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Notebook page",body="They painted an arrow to the exit, then shifted the barrier beyond the last turn. I walked back for my mother, who cannot climb the ditch. By then the painted arrow was covered and the man with the clipboard said he had seen no one.",anchor={scene="RVSDeadEnd"}},
-- T0367
{id="t0367-01",kind="written",pieces={"notebook"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="vehicle",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Logbook entry",body="I wrote that trial workers complained about waxy coating on plants.\n\nThe crew foreman felt dizzy after the second sprayer run.\n\nClover near the test fields had the same strange residue.",anchor={scene="RVSFlippedCrash"}},
{id="t0367-02",kind="written",pieces={"letter"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="vehicle",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Handwritten letter",body="A folded page inside the cab has the names of people assigned seats. Somebody crossed the whole column through and wrote “returned” above it. I saw the truck leave full. No one at the next road would say where its passengers had gone.",anchor={scene="RVSFlippedCrash"}},
-- T0368
{id="t0368-01",kind="set",pieces={"HandShovel","Bucket"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="vehicle",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="hand shovel and bucket",body="The hand shovel and bucket are tied with torn warning tape. The same number is marked on both. Dried blood lines the bucket. They were buried behind the checkpoint.",anchor={scene="RVSPoliceBlockade"}},
{id="t0368-02",kind="written",pieces={"notepad"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="vehicle",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Notepad page",body="A farm truck carried sacks from the test plot, with yellow dust on the seams. A torn sack left a stripe across the dirt road, and the grass where it fell had withered by evening.",anchor={scene="RVSPoliceBlockade"}},
-- T0369
{id="t0369-01",kind="written",pieces={"photograph"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="vehicle",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Annotated photograph",body="On the back: \"a greasy sheen in the cab after the greenhouse spray test. my wrists blistered. the tomato leaves went black within a day.\"",anchor={scene="RVSPoliceBlockadeShooting"}},
{id="t0369-02",kind="written",pieces={"notebook"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="vehicle",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Notebook page",body="I helped move the injured away from the barrier. Later an officer asked for the number of cars, not the number of people. He drew a fresh line under his total while two families were still behind the disabled van.",anchor={scene="RVSPoliceBlockadeShooting"}},
-- T0370
{id="t0370-01",kind="set",pieces={"FirstAidKit","WaterBottle"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="vehicle",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="First-aid kit and water bottle",body="Emerald flecks from the feed test are on the kit and the bottle. I think they were packed before the noon siren sounded.",anchor={scene="RVSRegionalProfessionVehicle"}},
{id="t0370-02",kind="written",pieces={"letter"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="vehicle",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Handwritten letter",body="The service driver showed me a card saying she could cross because her trade was needed. At the barrier they let the van through but asked her helper to wait. She had no line for him on the roster, only a place for the tools.",anchor={scene="RVSRegionalProfessionVehicle"}},
-- T0371
{id="t0371-01",kind="written",pieces={"receipt"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="vehicle",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Paper receipt",body="Feed, soap, and a clean jar, paid cash. My note below says brown foam came from the fertilizer trial.\n\nOur cat hid from the water bowl, and the foam ring was still on the rim.",anchor={scene="RVSRichJerk"}},
{id="t0371-02",kind="written",pieces={"notepad"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="vehicle",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Notepad page",body="He offered cash to get the road opened while the rest of us waited. The attendant counted the seats in his car and let him go. By morning our line had been listed as empty, though we had never moved.",anchor={scene="RVSRichJerk"}},
-- T0372
{id="t0372-01",kind="set",pieces={"Potato","EmptyJar"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="vehicle",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Potato and empty jar",body="Chalky water from the orchard treatment is on the potato and soil jar. I think they were packed before the crossing was barricaded.",anchor={scene="RVSRoadKill"}},
{id="t0372-02",kind="written",pieces={"notebook"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="vehicle",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Notebook page",body="The highway worker kept a tally of cars that stopped beside the dead animal. He was ordered to leave out the cars that turned around before reaching the barrier. My uncle was in one of those cars; we found his blanket by the milepost.",anchor={scene="RVSRoadKill"}},
-- T0373
{id="t0373-01",kind="written",pieces={"notebook"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="vehicle",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Notebook page",body="My cab entry says the pasture treatment workers brushed off mustard-colored dust.\n\nNot one fly remained on the trough, and the cows stood well back from it.",anchor={scene="RVSTrailerCrash"}},
{id="t0373-02",kind="written",pieces={"letter"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="vehicle",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Handwritten letter",body="I watched them seal the trailer, then ask the driver to take the family home by a route that had already closed. He asked for the children to be counted with the cargo because the passenger column was full. Nobody laughed.",anchor={scene="RVSTrailerCrash"}},
-- T0374
{id="t0374-01",kind="set",pieces={"Mop","Bucket"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="vehicle",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Mop and bucket",body="The mop and bucket are tied together with torn warning tape. A paper tag with just a number hangs from the knot. I think there's a stamp smudged on the bucket.",anchor={scene="RVSUtilityVehicle"}},
{id="t0374-02",kind="written",pieces={"notepad"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="vehicle",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Notepad page",body="A crew carried a tank used on the trial rows, still damp around the valve. I saw a worker rinse his hands in a ditch that flows toward the houses. The grass along that ditch was yellow.",anchor={scene="RVSUtilityVehicle"}},
-- T0375
{id="t0375-01",kind="written",pieces={"photograph"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="ground",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Photograph with note",body="On the back: “the second evening, an acrid film in the weathered bundle after the insecticide test. the tomato plants curled by dark.”",anchor={scene="RZSBBQParty"}},
{id="t0375-02",kind="written",pieces={"notebook"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="ground",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Notebook page",body="The party stayed after the announced closing time because the official road out was marked open on the paper. When the cars got there, a worker said the paper was from yesterday. We used it to start the fire when the night turned cold.",anchor={scene="RZSBBQParty"}},
-- T0376
{id="t0376-01",kind="set",pieces={"Battery","RadioBlack"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="ground",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Battery and radio",body="The battery and radio are packed together. Both are tacky and smell medicinal. It looks like something from a livestock supplement test.",anchor={scene="RZSBaseball"}},
{id="t0376-02",kind="written",pieces={"letter"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="ground",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Letter",body="They promised a ride for everyone still at the field after the game. The volunteer wrote down jerseys instead of names and told two siblings in ordinary clothes to wait. The bus left with empty seats and the list said full.",anchor={scene="RZSBaseball"}},
-- T0377
{id="t0377-01",kind="written",pieces={"receipt"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="ground",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Receipt with note",body="Feed, soap, and a clean jar, paid cash. My note below says violet powder came from the well-water study.\n\nThe mice abandoned the bin, and the powder was still on the lid.",anchor={scene="RZSBeachParty"}},
{id="t0377-02",kind="written",pieces={"notepad"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="ground",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Notepad page",body="A handwritten note beside the coolers says the coastal road was open through sundown. Someone came back for a forgotten shoe after dark and found the gate shut. The person responsible for the sign had gone home with the only key.",anchor={scene="RZSBeachParty"}},
-- T0378
{id="t0378-01",kind="set",pieces={"Axe","SeedBag"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="ground",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Axe and seed bag",body="The axe and seed bag have saltlike grains on them. They came from the test sprayer run last week. I grabbed them before the crops started withering.",anchor={scene="RZSBurntWreck"}},
{id="t0378-02",kind="written",pieces={"notebook"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="ground",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Notebook page",body="The car had a windshield pass for a route officially clear of traffic. At the next crossing the guards had a revised list and would not honor it. The driver folded the pass into quarters to keep it dry for his wife.",anchor={scene="RZSBurntWreck"}},
-- T0379
{id="t0379-01",kind="written",pieces={"notebook"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="ground",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Notebook page",body="My weathered bundle entry says the crop trial workers brushed off rust-colored grit.\n\nThe chickens stopped moving, and the grit lay in rust-colored streaks across the yard.",anchor={scene="RZSBuryingCamp"}},
{id="t0379-02",kind="written",pieces={"letter"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="ground",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Letter",body="I wrote down who we buried because the visitors collecting the numbers had counted tents instead of people. They asked for the notebook and left me the page for supplies. I kept this page folded under the coffee tin.",anchor={scene="RZSBuryingCamp"}},
-- T0380
{id="t0380-01",kind="set",pieces={"Bread","CannedCorn"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="ground",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Bread and canned corn",body="Wrapped bread and canned corn are tied with torn yellow-black tape. A numbered tag hangs from the knot, same number as on the tape. I think they were handed out before they closed off the route.",anchor={scene="RZSCampsite"}},
{id="t0380-02",kind="written",pieces={"notepad"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="ground",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Notepad page",body="We pitched the tent beyond the trial orchard, well outside the sprayed rows. Rain ran down the canvas and left the same yellow dust on our cups. My daughter had not eaten anything from the orchard.",anchor={scene="RZSCampsite"}},
-- T0381
{id="t0381-01",kind="written",pieces={"photograph"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="ground",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Photograph with note",body="On the back: “friday at closing, silver specks in the weathered bundle after the feed test. the ditch smelled metallic, and the minnows were floating.”",anchor={scene="RZSCharcoalBurner"}},
{id="t0381-02",kind="written",pieces={"notebook"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="ground",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Notebook page",body="The ranger had given us a route out and said to keep the slip clean. A second ranger came before dark and told us the route had never been assigned. We used the old slip for tinder, except this corner with my mother’s name.",anchor={scene="RZSCharcoalBurner"}},
-- T0382
{id="t0382-01",kind="set",pieces={"Fertilizer","GardeningSprayEmpty"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="ground",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Fertilizer sack and sprayer",body="The fertilizer sack and empty sprayer are packed together. A greasy sheen crusts the nozzle and weeps from the sack seam. Looks like it's from a fertilizer trial.",anchor={scene="RZSDean"}},
{id="t0382-02",kind="written",pieces={"letter"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="ground",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Letter",body="Our camp was told the pickup would stop where the smoke could be seen. A vehicle came, copied the number of tents, and drove away before the sleeping people woke. The next day someone had crossed our site off the rescue map.",anchor={scene="RZSDean"}},
-- T0383
{id="t0383-01",kind="written",pieces={"receipt"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="ground",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Receipt with note",body="Feed, soap, and a clean jar, paid cash. My note below says emerald flecks came from the orchard treatment.\n\nThe horse kicked away its feed, and the flecks lay on the trough water like pollen.",anchor={scene="RZSFishingTrip"}},
{id="t0383-02",kind="written",pieces={"notepad"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="ground",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Notepad page",body="The fishing party was told to wait for a boat after the bridge closed. A patrol crossed upstream with room aboard, but its passenger sheet was filled out already. We waved a tackle box until our arms hurt.",anchor={scene="RZSFishingTrip"}},
-- T0384
{id="t0384-01",kind="set",pieces={"KeyRing","Bucket"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="ground",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Key ring and bucket",body="The key ring and bucket are packed together. Brown foam has dried on both, with a high-water line in the bucket. I think it's from a pasture treatment.",anchor={scene="RZSForestCamp"}},
{id="t0384-02",kind="set",pieces={"RadioReceiver","Map","Pills"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="ground",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Receiver, map and pills",body="A receiver still set to an emergency band, and a strip of pills. The road map has the county roads crossed out in one neat hand. The campers seem to have left before any closure was announced.",anchor={scene="RZSForestCamp"}},
-- T0385
{id="t0385-01",kind="written",pieces={"notebook"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="ground",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Notebook page",body="My weathered bundle entry says the experimental seed run workers brushed off chalky water. my throat tightened before county trucks reached us.\n\nNo one wanted to keep the wet copy. It dried unevenly, and the ink from the first entry stayed visible beneath the second.\n\nThe younger one wanted to throw it away. I promised we would ask in the morning, and put it where neither of us could forget.",anchor={scene="RZSForestCampEaten"}},
{id="t0385-02",kind="written",pieces={"letter"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="ground",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Letter",body="I was told everyone here had been collected in the morning. I still heard my neighbor calling from the other tent when the men packed up their list. I wrote her name where their pencil had left a blank.",anchor={scene="RZSForestCampEaten"}},
-- T0386
{id="t0386-01",kind="set",pieces={"FirstAidKit","WaterBottle"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="ground",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="first-aid kit and water bottle",body="The first-aid kit and water bottle are bound with a tag. The tag lists a shelter code that's been crossed out twice. Medical supplies are missing from inside the kit.",anchor={scene="RZSHermitCamp"}},
{id="t0386-02",kind="written",pieces={"notepad"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="ground",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Notepad page",body="The old man had no part in the farm trial, yet a yellow rim formed around his water pail after the storm. He kept the first pail for washing and gave guests the second. The stream comes down from the same treated slope.",anchor={scene="RZSHermitCamp"}},
-- T0387
{id="t0387-01",kind="written",pieces={"photograph"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="ground",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Photograph with note",body="On the back: “a cloying orchard smell in the weathered bundle after the livestock supplement test. my sister coughed all night. the ewes would not graze the sprayed edge.”",anchor={scene="RZSHillbillyHoedown"}},
{id="t0387-02",kind="written",pieces={"notebook"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="ground",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Notebook page",body="We counted people for a ride home by the pairs on the dance card. The driver was instructed to use the official total, two fewer than ours. He asked the two without partners to stand by the road until another truck came.",anchor={scene="RZSHillbillyHoedown"}},
-- T0388
{id="t0388-01",kind="set",pieces={"Potato","EmptyJar"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="ground",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Potato and empty jar",body="The potato has a waxy film that won't rinse off. The empty jar smells like the crop spray from last week. I've never seen residue this thick before.",anchor={scene="RZSHunterCamp"}},
{id="t0388-02",kind="written",pieces={"letter"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="ground",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Letter",body="The group came back to find a notice saying the camp had been cleared. Their boots were still here and the fire was warm. I carried the notice along the trail because I knew the youngest had gone for water.",anchor={scene="RZSHunterCamp"}},
-- T0389
{id="t0389-01",kind="written",pieces={"receipt"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="corpse",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Receipt with note",body="Feed, soap, and a clean jar, paid cash. My note below says a medicinal odor came from the sprayer trial.\n\nThe driver grew dizzy at dawn, and the verge grass he walked through had gone gray.",anchor={scene="RZSMurderScene"}},
{id="t0389-02",kind="written",pieces={"notepad"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="corpse",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Notepad page",body="I heard three shots, then the person taking statements told me the file would say two. He said the third sound might have come from a car door. I put a mark beside it, because the woman on the ground heard it too.",anchor={scene="RZSMurderScene"}},
-- T0390
{id="t0390-01",kind="set",pieces={"Mop","Bucket"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="ground",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Mop and bucket",body="The mop and bucket carry violet powder, maybe from the crop trial. They were packed before the back road closed.",anchor={scene="RZSMusicFest"}},
{id="t0390-02",kind="written",pieces={"notebook"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="ground",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Notebook page",body="The festival volunteers were asked to count exits while the music still played. The man at the gate kept the old total when the rear fence came down. He said correcting it would delay the buses.",anchor={scene="RZSMusicFest"}},
-- T0391
{id="t0391-01",kind="written",pieces={"notebook"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="ground",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Notebook page",body="My weathered bundle entry says the greenhouse test workers brushed off saltlike grains. my wrists blistered before the telephone line died.\n\nMy mother put it with the household bills so it would not be thrown away. It was the only part of the week that still had a date.\n\nSomeone had to finish the household list even though the office had closed. I wrote the names in the space left for expenses.",anchor={scene="RZSMusicFestStage"}},
{id="t0391-02",kind="written",pieces={"letter"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="ground",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Letter",body="The singer stopped to tell the crowd where the exit was. A marshal took the microphone and pointed in the other direction, toward the closed service lane. The next morning the printed directions still showed the first exit.",anchor={scene="RZSMusicFestStage"}},
-- T0392
{id="t0392-01",kind="set",pieces={"Battery","RadioBlack"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="ground",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Battery and radio",body="The battery is bound to the radio with torn warning tape. The dial is taped fixed on one channel. A cut strap looks like where a response tag was removed.",anchor={scene="RZSNastyMattress"}},
{id="t0392-02",kind="written",pieces={"notepad"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="ground",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Notepad page",body="The woman had been sleeping beside a field where the trial sprayers passed at dawn. She moved her bedding when the smell reached it, but the pale film returned overnight. Nobody in camp had seen a warning sign.",anchor={scene="RZSNastyMattress"}},
-- T0393
{id="t0393-01",kind="written",pieces={"photograph"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="ground",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Photograph with note",body="On the back: “saturday before sunrise, waxy pollen on the weathered bundle after the fertilizer trial. our cat would not drink from the water bowl; a pale film sat on top. the seedlings by the fence went limp by noon.”\n\nA pencil line had been rubbed thin but not erased. I could still read enough of it to see which field the trial had been in.\n\nIt may have started elsewhere; none of us saw the beginning. I only know what had reached our rows by then.",anchor={scene="RZSOccultActivity"}},
{id="t0393-02",kind="written",pieces={"notebook"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="ground",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Notebook page",body="They gathered here after the road was closed, and someone carefully counted every person present. The official tally for this stretch was zero. The woman with the candles made a second list on the back of a wrapper.",anchor={scene="RZSOccultActivity"}},
-- T0394
{id="t0394-01",kind="set",pieces={"Axe","SeedBag"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="ground",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="axe and seed bag",body="The axe and seed bag have silver specks on them. I think they're from the orchard treatment. The residue wasn't in the application instructions.",anchor={scene="RZSOldFirepit"}},
{id="t0394-02",kind="written",pieces={"letter"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="ground",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Letter",body="The group burned the map after the marked road failed them. One corner survived with an arrow pointing to a station that had stopped taking arrivals. I recognized my own handwriting on the corner; I had copied the directions from a uniformed man.",anchor={scene="RZSOldFirepit"}},
-- T0396
{id="t0396-01",kind="written",pieces={"diary"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="ground",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Diary page",body="Tuesday: the pasture-test workers slept here with gray foam on their boots. The creek tasted bitter, and the grass along it had gone pale where they rinsed their tanks.\n\nI wrote down which pasture rows had browned while I could still remember them.\n\nThere may be a simple reason for the change. Nobody I asked knew what the foam was.",anchor={scene="RZSOldShelter"}},
{id="t0396-02",kind="written",pieces={"notebook"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="ground",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Notebook page",body="We stayed under this roof because the trail below was listed as an evacuation route. A runner came back saying the gate at its end had been chained before noon. I left a dry blanket here for whoever believed the same sign.",anchor={scene="RZSOldShelter"}},
-- T0397
{id="t0397-01",kind="set",pieces={"WaterBottle","EmptyJar"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="ground",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Water bottle and jar",body="A cloudy water bottle and a sample jar share a waxy green film. A scrap of twine around both still holds treated pasture grass.",anchor={scene="RZSOrphanedFawn"}},
{id="t0397-02",kind="written",pieces={"letter"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="ground",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Letter",body="The ranger brought the fawn to the road and asked for a wildlife pickup. The checkpoint worker recorded one animal and no people, though the child holding its blanket stood beside him. She was still there when they shut the lane.",anchor={scene="RZSOrphanedFawn"}},
-- T0398
{id="t0398-01",kind="written",pieces={"notepad"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="ground",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Notepad page",body="Personal note: the insecticide crew crossed at dawn, leaving yellow dust on the grass. The deer fled, and by afternoon the clover where they had grazed was dull and curled.\n\nI saved it from the rubbish bag because the back lists the plots they treated.\n\nIt could be a mistake in the copying. The sprayer tanks stacked beside the page were real enough, and still half full.",anchor={scene="RZSRangerSmith"}},
{id="t0398-02",kind="written",pieces={"notepad"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="ground",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Notepad page",body="The north trail was marked clear after the patrol turned back halfway. I asked why my brother’s campsite appeared on the completed section. The ranger said the box only had room for one kind of mark.",anchor={scene="RZSRangerSmith"}},
-- T0399
{id="t0399-01",kind="set",pieces={"Battery","RadioBlack"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="ground",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="battery and black radio",body="I found a battery and black radio in the spray barn. Red field dust clogs the speaker vents. The dial is sticky with dried chemical residue.",anchor={scene="RZSRockerParty"}},
{id="t0399-02",kind="written",pieces={"notebook"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="ground",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Notebook page",body="A road crew passed the gathering and said there would be transport at daylight. The handwritten passenger list filled before the first vehicle arrived. The musicians kept playing so the people at the far end would not hear the argument.",anchor={scene="RZSRockerParty"}},
-- T0400
{id="t0400-01",kind="written",pieces={"letter"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="ground",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Letter",body="I kept the gloves with blue powder from the seed trial. Our dog stopped drinking from the ditch, and the barley rows beside it were speckled blue.\n\nThe person beside me recognized the handwriting of whoever had mixed the seed treatment, and went quiet.\n\nThe person who was supposed to collect it had no time to stop. I did not put it back with the rest of the ordinary papers.",anchor={scene="RZSSadCamp"}},
{id="t0400-02",kind="written",pieces={"letter"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="ground",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Letter",body="The camp had four spaces marked on the board but five people sleeping under the canvas. The volunteer tried to add one line after the supply truck departed. Someone had already sent the board’s total onward.",anchor={scene="RZSSadCamp"}},
-- T0401
{id="t0401-01",kind="set",pieces={"Garbagebag","Gloves_LeatherGloves"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="ground",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Gloves in a trash bag",body="Leather gloves sit inside a knotted trash sack. Mustard-colored crop dust coats the cuffs. The outside of the sack is clean.",anchor={scene="RZSSexyTime"}},
{id="t0401-02",kind="written",pieces={"notepad"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="ground",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Notepad page",body="They left in a hurry when a patrol announced this area was clear. One of them went back for a coat, and the patrol told her no one had been here since morning. The date on the coat label was today.",anchor={scene="RZSSexyTime"}},
-- T0402
{id="t0402-01",kind="written",pieces={"notebook"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="ground",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Notebook page",body="My entry says the orchard crew rinsed its sprayer upstream. The water turned milky, and my hands blistered where the irrigation ran across the beds.\n\nI thought the date would settle it. Every row we watered that week yellowed from the edges in.\n\nI wrote the time before I went back for the others. The clock may have been slow.",anchor={scene="RZSSurvivalistCamp"}},
{id="t0402-02",kind="written",pieces={"notebook"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="ground",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Notebook page",body="The survivalist had packed for a three-day hike along the official safe corridor. At its first crossing a new barrier sent him back toward the town he had left. He wrote the change in the margin so he would not trust the printed route again.",anchor={scene="RZSSurvivalistCamp"}},
-- T0403
{id="t0403-01",kind="set",pieces={"Bread","CannedCorn"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="ground",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Bread and canned corn",body="A wrapped loaf and a can of corn have the same pale field dust. The loaf is tied with twine, I think from a treated seed sack.",anchor={scene="RZSTragicPicnic"}},
{id="t0403-02",kind="written",pieces={"letter"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="ground",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Letter",body="At the picnic we were told a vehicle would come for each household. The first driver counted blankets spread on the grass instead. My little niece carried none, so I wrote her name twice to make sure she was seen.",anchor={scene="RZSTragicPicnic"}},
-- T0404
{id="t0404-01",kind="written",pieces={"photograph"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="ground",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Photograph with note",body="On the back: “No animals after the pasture trial sprayed. The sharp smell reached camp before the noon siren.”\n\nThe first account was spoken quickly, as if there might be a bus to catch. I wrote it down before another person could replace it.\n\nThe younger one wanted to throw it away. I promised we would ask in the morning, and put it where neither of us could forget.",anchor={scene="RZSTrapperCamp"}},
{id="t0404-02",kind="written",pieces={"notepad"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="ground",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Notepad page",body="The trapper was asked to clear the path for evacuation and left his traps open as instructed. The promised vehicles never used it. He went back at dusk to close the traps so no one walking in the dark would be hurt.",anchor={scene="RZSTrapperCamp"}},
-- T0405
{id="t0405-01",kind="set",pieces={"KeyRing","FirstAidKit"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="vehicle",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Van keys and first-aid kit",body="The van keys and first-aid kit share one cord. Green field flecks mark the keys. A strip of road tape seals the kit.",anchor={scene="RZSVanCamp"}},
{id="t0405-02",kind="set",pieces={"Rope","Gloves_LeatherGloves","MeasuringTape"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="vehicle",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Rope, gloves and measuring tape",body="Rope cut in equal lengths, leather gloves, a measuring tape. The tape stops at the same mark each time. Perimeter around the checkpoint vans. Too small for the evacuation crowd.",anchor={scene="RZSVanCamp"}},
-- T0406
{id="t0406-01",kind="written",pieces={"receipt"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="ground",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Receipt with note",body="Soap, work gloves, and two sample jars, paid cash. My note says the fertilizer crew left oily residue here before the road was closed.\n\nWe needed the supplies listed here for the following morning. The people who took the count left without asking whether we had them.\n\nIt may have started elsewhere; none of us saw the beginning. I only know what had reached this place before they closed the road.",anchor={scene="RZSWasteDump"}},
{id="t0406-02",kind="written",pieces={"letter"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="ground",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Letter",body="The hauler was told the dump road was clear and took a detour to avoid the crowded main route. The gate had been welded shut that morning. He wrote down the time because the dispatch sheet still charged him for arriving late.",anchor={scene="RZSWasteDump"}},
-- T0407
{id="t0407-01",kind="set",pieces={"Bucket","WaterBottle"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="ground",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Bucket and water bottle",body="A bucket and water bottle hold the same yellow scum. Dried irrigation water left the same crust in the field ditch. Dead corn covers every acre I can see from the porch.",anchor={scene="RZSWaterPump"}},
{id="t0407-02",kind="written",pieces={"notepad"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="ground",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Notepad page",body="They shut the pump after assigning the households one pail apiece. More people came from the road, but their names belonged to a different district on the list. My father shared his pail while the clerk went to find another page.",anchor={scene="RZSWaterPump"}},
-- T0408
{id="t0408-01",kind="set",pieces={"Map","Pencil"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Map and pencil",body="I see a road rubbed out on the map, with six small figures beside it. The pencil has worn through the paper where I think they waited. The date is on the wrapper, not the map."},
{id="t0408-02",kind="set",pieces={"Clipboard","Eraser"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Clipboard and eraser",body="I found a clipboard listing four vehicles and departure times. The eraser sits next to where a fifth line was removed. Small handwriting is still pressed into the paper there."},
{id="t0408-03",kind="set",pieces={"FirstAidKit","BathTowel"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="First-aid kit and towel",body="The sealed kit is tied to a towel marked for a passenger. The seat is crossed off, though the towel is still damp. There's a hurried thumbprint on the corner."},
{id="t0408-04",kind="set",pieces={"Map","SheetPaper2"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Map and loose page",body="The loose page shows a different route than the map. Someone traced both with a finger stained from a lunch wrapper. One edge was kept dry beneath a coat."},
{id="t0408-05",kind="set",pieces={"HandTorch","Battery"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Torch and battery",body="The battery is taped to a torch beside a handwritten departure time. I think the owner waited long enough to use up the spare. A short tally was added after the bundle was tied."},
{id="t0408-06",kind="set",pieces={"Badge","RubberBand"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Badge and rubber band",body="A badge and a band for counting arrivals are tied together. The band has an extra notch that isn't on the badge. The string has been retied since morning."},
{id="t0408-07",kind="set",pieces={"Jack","LugWrench"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Jack and lug wrench",body="The jack has fresh road grit and the wrench a strip of warning tape. The repair looks abandoned beside a penciled clearance time. The date is on the wrapper, not on the tools."},
{id="t0408-08",kind="set",pieces={"WalkieTalkie1","Pencil"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Radio and pencil",body="A frequency is scratched into the pencil's paint. The radio's label names another channel, and its paper says to wait. A strip of cloth keeps the pair together."},
{id="t0408-09",kind="set",pieces={"Notebook","RedPen"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Notebook and red pen",body="Six names in the notebook, listed for pickup. The red pen adds one more but runs out before finishing. There's a thumbprint smudged in the margin."},
{id="t0408-10",kind="set",pieces={"Bag_Schoolbag","Map"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Schoolbag and map",body="The bag holds an unused lunch wrapper. The map is folded to a stop crossed out twice. A child wrote the original time on the strap."},
-- T0409
{id="t0409-01",kind="set",pieces={"EmptyJar","SeedBag"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Jar and seed sack",body="Yellow grains crust the jar's rim and a torn seed sack tied to it. The sack's label names a test plot. The string has been retied since morning."},
{id="t0409-02",kind="set",pieces={"WaterBottle","Bucket"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Water bottle and bucket",body="A water bottle and a bucket share a chalk mark. The bucket holds numbered tags with tape on each. I think a patrol marked them before the road closed."},
{id="t0409-03",kind="set",pieces={"Gloves_LeatherGloves","GardeningSprayEmpty"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Gloves and sprayer",body="The leather gloves still reek of whatever was in the spray. Empty now, but the label mentions crop treatment trials. Whoever wore these left in a panic."},
{id="t0409-04",kind="set",pieces={"AnimalFeedBag","Bucket"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Feed sack and bucket",body="The feed sack has an oily patch where it leaned against the sprayer. The bucket carries a chemical film above its waterline. Both were stored in the equipment shed."},
{id="t0409-05",kind="set",pieces={"SeedBag","DuctTape"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Seed sack and tape",body="Tape seals a slit in the seed sack, but pale dust sits on the outside. A child's height is marked on the tape. A short tally was added after the bundle was tied."},
{id="t0409-06",kind="set",pieces={"EmptyJar","Map"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Jar and map",body="The empty jar has a tape label with a number. The map shows the same number at a checkpoint. Someone drew a closure line through that road."},
{id="t0409-07",kind="set",pieces={"Bread","DishCloth"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Bread and dish cloth",body="The loaf is wrapped in a dish cloth, the knot still tied. A tag on the cloth carries a ration number. It matches the ration lists they read out at the checkpoint."},
{id="t0409-08",kind="set",pieces={"Soap2","Sponge"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Soap and sponge",body="The soap and sponge are in a bag with a numbered tag. A handwritten order says one per person, list every name. The count is crossed out and the checkpoint is closed."},
{id="t0409-09",kind="set",pieces={"GardeningSprayEmpty","Postcard"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Empty sprayer and postcard",body="The card asks for supper to be kept warm. A ring from a sprayer runs across the writing. There are fine pale grains in the fold."},
{id="t0409-10",kind="set",pieces={"Fertilizer","GlassTumbler"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Fertilizer and drinking glass",body="There are fine grains on the rim of the glass. The fertilizer sack beside it is sealed with household thread."},
-- T0410
{id="t0410-01",kind="set",pieces={"Map","Pencil"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Map and pencil",body="A road is rubbed out on the map, with six small figures beside it. The pencil has worn through the paper where they waited."},
{id="t0410-02",kind="set",pieces={"Clipboard","Eraser"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Clipboard and eraser",body="The clipboard has four routes listed with times. Someone took the eraser to a fifth one. I can still see a child's writing beneath it."},
{id="t0410-03",kind="set",pieces={"FirstAidKit","BathTowel"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="First aid kit and towel",body="A sealed first-aid kit is tied to a towel marked with a seat number. The number is crossed off and the seal is unbroken. I think it was loaded for a vehicle that left without it."},
{id="t0410-04",kind="set",pieces={"Map","SheetPaper2"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Map and loose page",body="The loose page shows a different route from the one inked on the map. Someone traced both with a finger stained from a lunch wrapper."},
{id="t0410-05",kind="set",pieces={"HandTorch","Battery"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Torch and battery",body="The battery is taped to a torch beside a handwritten departure time. Whoever it belonged to waited long enough to use up the spare."},
{id="t0410-06",kind="set",pieces={"Badge","RubberBand"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Badge and rubber band",body="A badge and a band for counting arrivals are tied together. The band has an extra notch that never made it onto the badge."},
{id="t0410-07",kind="set",pieces={"Jack","LugWrench"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Jack and lug wrench",body="The jack has fresh road grit and the wrench has warning tape. The repair was left unfinished beside a penciled clearance time."},
{id="t0410-08",kind="set",pieces={"WalkieTalkie1","Pencil"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Radio and pencil",body="A frequency is scratched into the pencil's paint. The radio's label names another channel. The paper wrapped around it says to wait."},
{id="t0410-09",kind="set",pieces={"Notebook","RedPen"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Notebook and red pen",body="The notebook lists six households with bus assignments. A red pen adds one more name partway through. It runs dry before the pickup time is filled in."},
{id="t0410-10",kind="set",pieces={"Bag_Schoolbag","Map"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Schoolbag and map",body="The map marks three safe zones, each one crossed out in pen. Instructions are crumpled inside the schoolbag's main pocket. Someone changed the meeting time twice by hand."},
-- T0411
{id="t0411-01",kind="set",pieces={"EmptyJar","SeedBag"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Empty jar and seed bag",body="Jar's caked with dried pesticide residue inside. Seed bag says trial formula from the county extension office. There's a whole case of these in the barn outside."},
{id="t0411-02",kind="set",pieces={"WaterBottle","Bucket"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Water bottle and bucket",body="A clean bottle and a cloudy bucket share a chalk mark. The bucket was filled far from the rows after the sprayer passed."},
{id="t0411-03",kind="set",pieces={"Gloves_LeatherGloves","GardeningSprayEmpty"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Leather gloves and empty sprayer",body="The leather gloves are stained yellow-brown around the fingers. The spray can is bone dry but reeks of chemicals. Someone was working fields when things went wrong."},
{id="t0411-04",kind="set",pieces={"AnimalFeedBag","Bucket"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Feed sack and bucket",body="The feed sack has an oily streak under its fold. A rinse pail has the same mark above the waterline."},
{id="t0411-05",kind="set",pieces={"SeedBag","DuctTape"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Seed bag and duct tape",body="Tape seals a slit in the seed sack. The pale dust under it has caught on the outside. A child's height is marked on the tape."},
{id="t0411-06",kind="set",pieces={"EmptyJar","Map"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Empty jar and map",body="The empty jar has checkpoint tape and tag 5 on it. The map has the evacuation route marked with a thick line. A scribbled order on the map says to stay quiet."},
{id="t0411-07",kind="set",pieces={"Bread","DishCloth"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Bread and dish cloth",body="The loaf is in clean cloth, tied and sealed with barrier tape. A numbered tag under the tape has a checkpoint code and initials. I think I've seen tags like this on belongings at the perimeter."},
{id="t0411-08",kind="set",pieces={"Soap2","Sponge"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="soap and sponge",body="The soap is worn down on one side and the sponge is dry. They're wrapped in barrier tape with a cup. A numbered tag is tied to the package."},
{id="t0411-09",kind="set",pieces={"GardeningSprayEmpty","Postcard"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Empty sprayer and postcard",body="The card asks for supper to be kept warm. A ring from a sprayer runs across it, and the ink looks fresh."},
{id="t0411-10",kind="set",pieces={"Fertilizer","GlassTumbler"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Fertilizer and tumbler",body="Residue crusted in the tumbler. Half the fertilizer is gone from the bag. Someone measured out doses here."},
-- T0412
{id="t0412-01",kind="set",pieces={"Map","Pencil"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Map and pencil",body="Pencil marks on the map show where checkpoints should have been. Half are crossed out. They changed the plan but never told anyone."},
{id="t0412-02",kind="set",pieces={"Clipboard","Eraser"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Clipboard and eraser",body="The clipboard lists four buses with times but no passenger counts. The eraser sits beside a smudged fifth line. I can still see where a child wrote their name."},
{id="t0412-03",kind="set",pieces={"FirstAidKit","BathTowel"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="First aid kit and towel",body="The sealed kit is tied to a towel marked for a passenger. The seat is crossed off, though the towel is still damp."},
{id="t0412-04",kind="set",pieces={"Map","SheetPaper2"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Map and loose page",body="The map shows safe zones circled. The loose page updates it—most crossed out. Greasy fingerprints on both."},
{id="t0412-05",kind="set",pieces={"HandTorch","Battery"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Torch and battery",body="The battery has someone's shift time written on it. The torch is still in the wrapper. They packed them but never made it to distribution."},
{id="t0412-06",kind="set",pieces={"Badge","RubberBand"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Badge and rubber band",body="The badge clip is gone. Someone used a rubber band to wear it. It's stretched thin with marks from fingers that kept adjusting it."},
{id="t0412-07",kind="set",pieces={"Jack","LugWrench"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Jack and lug wrench",body="The lug wrench has a zone tag still zip-tied to it. The jack sits on a clipboard with routes crossed out in red. Someone dropped their gear mid-shift."},
{id="t0412-08",kind="set",pieces={"WalkieTalkie1","Pencil"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Radio and pencil",body="A name is worn off the pencil's paint. The walkie talkie died on channel two. They kept logging zones after it went silent."},
{id="t0412-09",kind="set",pieces={"Notebook","RedPen"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Notebook and red pen",body="The notebook lists families by bus route, tally ending at six. The red pen adds one more name. It ran dry before writing the seat."},
{id="t0412-10",kind="set",pieces={"Bag_Schoolbag","Map"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Schoolbag and map",body="Official zones are circled on the map in red marker. The schoolbag has checkpoint times written inside in a child's hand. Three of those zones were already gone by the last entry."},
-- T0413
{id="t0413-01",kind="set",pieces={"EmptyJar","SeedBag"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Empty jar and seed bag",body="The jar's coated with dust from the seed bag. Its label lists a test plot number. Both are bound together in roadside mud."},
{id="t0413-02",kind="set",pieces={"WaterBottle","Bucket"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Water bottle and bucket",body="The water bottle sits beside a bucket marked with white chalk. The bucket holds cloudy water from beyond the crop rows."},
{id="t0413-03",kind="set",pieces={"Gloves_LeatherGloves","GardeningSprayEmpty"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Leather gloves and empty sprayer",body="One leather glove has brownish dust, the other is cleaner. The empty gardening spray sat outside a garden fence. Whatever was in the fields got carried here."},
{id="t0413-04",kind="set",pieces={"AnimalFeedBag","Bucket"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Feed sack and bucket",body="The animal feed bag shows a chemical residue I don't recognize. The bucket has the same coating dried inside. Strange to find them this far from any field."},
{id="t0413-05",kind="set",pieces={"SeedBag","DuctTape"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Seed bag and duct tape",body="Tape seals a slit in the seed sack. The pale treated-seed dust has caught on the outside. A child's height is marked on it."},
{id="t0413-06",kind="set",pieces={"EmptyJar","Map"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Empty jar and map",body="The empty jar reeks of pesticide. Field boundaries on the map are marked in the same sticky residue."},
{id="t0413-07",kind="set",pieces={"Bread","DishCloth"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Bread and dish cloth",body="The bread has a numbered tag pinned on. The dish cloth is marked with tape. I think it was handed out at a checkpoint."},
{id="t0413-08",kind="set",pieces={"Soap2","Sponge"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Soap and sponge",body="The soap and sponge hang from a guard's numbered tag. Tape on the shelf reads 'Do not enter, Zone 3'. An order on the tag says tell no one."},
{id="t0413-09",kind="set",pieces={"GardeningSprayEmpty","Postcard"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Empty sprayer and postcard",body="The postcard lists field testing schedules. The empty sprayer beside it reeks of chemicals. Someone brought their work home."},
{id="t0413-10",kind="set",pieces={"Fertilizer","GlassTumbler"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Fertilizer and drinking glass",body="I found the glass half-full of dissolved fertilizer. This is nowhere near the fields they were supposed to spray."},
-- T0414
{id="t0414-01",kind="set",pieces={"Map","Pencil"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Map and pencil",body="Pencil marks on the map tally people at checkpoints. Half are scratched out. Someone stopped updating it."},
{id="t0414-02",kind="set",pieces={"Clipboard","Eraser"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Clipboard and eraser",body="The clipboard lists four vehicle numbers, no names. Someone used the eraser on a fifth line. I can still make out a child's writing underneath."},
{id="t0414-03",kind="set",pieces={"FirstAidKit","BathTowel"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="First aid kit and towel",body="Someone wrapped this kit in a damp towel and ran. The tag says collected but it never made it on board. I found it in the grass outside."},
{id="t0414-04",kind="set",pieces={"Map","SheetPaper2"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Map and loose page",body="The map marks official shelter locations across the county. The page lists the same addresses with dates they were overrun. Someone's thumbprint smudged the ink on both."},
{id="t0414-05",kind="set",pieces={"HandTorch","Battery"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Torch and battery",body="Gate torch and battery, but they don't fit together. Same kit. Someone sat here for hours trying anyway."},
{id="t0414-06",kind="set",pieces={"Badge","RubberBand"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Badge and rubber band",body="A rubber band looped around this badge six times over. Each loop for one evacuation run, scrawled on the back. They got through five."},
{id="t0414-07",kind="set",pieces={"Jack","LugWrench"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Jack and lug wrench",body="The jack has checkpoint grit and the lug wrench has a route tag. Someone's name is scrawled on the evacuation log beside them."},
{id="t0414-08",kind="set",pieces={"WalkieTalkie1","Pencil"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Radio and pencil",body="The walkie talkie's battery is dead on the evacuation channel. Pencil marks on the case track days, then hours, then nothing. Nobody ever answered the call for rescue."},
{id="t0414-09",kind="set",pieces={"Notebook","RedPen"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Notebook and red pen",body="I see evacuation routes in the notebook, half crossed out. The red pen added six street names in rushed handwriting. It dried up halfway through someone's phone number."},
{id="t0414-10",kind="set",pieces={"Bag_Schoolbag","Map"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Schoolbag and map",body="The schoolbag has a class name tag still attached. The map shows routes they never opened for us. Someone circled our street in red ink."},
-- T0415
{id="t0415-01",kind="set",pieces={"EmptyJar","SeedBag"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Empty jar and seed bag",body="The jar's label marks a test plot. The seed bag is dusted the same yellow. Both lay in roadside mud, far from any field."},
{id="t0415-02",kind="set",pieces={"WaterBottle","Bucket"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Water bottle and bucket",body="The water bottle and bucket both have the same yellow dust. They sat beyond the last row where the sprayers never went."},
{id="t0415-03",kind="set",pieces={"Gloves_LeatherGloves","GardeningSprayEmpty"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Leather gloves and empty sprayer",body="The leather gloves show field dirt on one, soap on the other. The gardening spray is empty now. It went from the fields indoors."},
{id="t0415-04",kind="set",pieces={"AnimalFeedBag","Bucket"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Feed bag and bucket",body="The animal feed bag was by the sprayed crops. This bucket has the same residue coating it. The chemical drifted off the field."},
{id="t0415-05",kind="set",pieces={"SeedBag","DuctTape"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Seed bag and duct tape",body="Duct tape binds the seed bag in thick layers. I see warnings about treated contents beneath the wrap. Someone sealed this tight but the seeds made it to the ground."},
{id="t0415-06",kind="set",pieces={"EmptyJar","Map"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Empty jar and map",body="The jar's paper label names a trial row. The residue inside seems to match a plot marked on the map."},
{id="t0415-07",kind="set",pieces={"Bread","DishCloth"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="bread and dish cloth",body="The bread has a numbered tag pinned on. The dish cloth has tape marks and a name list stuck to it. It looks like a checkpoint handout."},
{id="t0415-08",kind="set",pieces={"Soap2","Sponge"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Soap and sponge",body="The soap has a numbered tag taped on. The sponge has a count written on it. I think it was a patrol handout."},
{id="t0415-09",kind="set",pieces={"GardeningSprayEmpty","Postcard"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Empty sprayer and postcard",body="A postcard outlines field sections for pesticide trials. The sprayer's bone dry but reeks of chemicals. Found them way past the marked boundaries."},
{id="t0415-10",kind="set",pieces={"Fertilizer","GlassTumbler"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Fertilizer and drinking glass",body="The drinking glass has powder caked inside. A fertilizer bag sits next to it on the path. Nobody farms here."},
-- T0416
{id="t0416-01",kind="set",pieces={"Map","Pencil"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Map and pencil",body="The map shows safe zones drawn in pencil. All of them scratched out hard. Someone wrote 'no pickup' beside every circle."},
{id="t0416-02",kind="set",pieces={"Clipboard","Eraser"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Clipboard and eraser",body="The clipboard lists four vehicle IDs and no names. Someone used the eraser on a fifth line. I can still make out a child's handwriting underneath."},
{id="t0416-03",kind="set",pieces={"FirstAidKit","BathTowel"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="First aid kit and towel",body="The first aid kit has a grid code on it. A bath towel is tied to it, someone's initials marked inside. Neither made it to where they were supposed to go."},
{id="t0416-04",kind="set",pieces={"Map","SheetPaper2"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Map and loose page",body="The map marks routes that the paper says were already blocked. Greasy prints cover both, like someone checked while eating. The official plan didn't account for what really happened."},
{id="t0416-05",kind="set",pieces={"HandTorch","Battery"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Torch and battery",body="The battery's taped to the torch with a staging number written on. I bet they dropped it sprinting when the convoy left without warning."},
{id="t0416-06",kind="set",pieces={"Badge","RubberBand"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Badge and rubber band",body="A rubber band's looped tight around this badge. Someone marked it every time they sent a group through. Way more marks than they ever admitted evacuating."},
{id="t0416-07",kind="set",pieces={"Jack","LugWrench"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Jack and lug wrench",body="The lug wrench has a zone code stamped into the metal. The jack's tagged for a convoy that never arrived. They documented everything so carefully."},
{id="t0416-08",kind="set",pieces={"WalkieTalkie1","Pencil"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Radio and pencil",body="I found rally points carved into the pencil. The walkie talkie's battery is still full. Nobody ever broadcast."},
{id="t0416-09",kind="set",pieces={"Notebook","RedPen"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Notebook and red pen",body="I see a notebook with six names. A red pen adds one more, runs out before the seat line."},
{id="t0416-10",kind="set",pieces={"Bag_Schoolbag","Map"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Schoolbag and map",body="The schoolbag still has its evacuation group sticker. The map shows a route to a shelter that doesn't exist anymore. A child marked the date they were supposed to leave."},
-- T0417
{id="t0417-01",kind="set",pieces={"EmptyJar","SeedBag"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Empty jar and seed bag",body="The empty jar and seed bag are knotted together with muddy string. I can read a test plot number on the jar's faded label. They're way out here on the roadside, nowhere near a field."},
{id="t0417-02",kind="set",pieces={"WaterBottle","Bucket"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Water bottle and bucket",body="I found a water bottle and bucket coated in fine dust. Both sat outside the marked plot. The trial spray reached too far."},
{id="t0417-03",kind="set",pieces={"Gloves_LeatherGloves","GardeningSprayEmpty"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Leather gloves and empty sprayer",body="One leather glove has field dust. The other has kitchen soap on it. The empty sprayer was carried indoors, I think."},
{id="t0417-04",kind="set",pieces={"AnimalFeedBag","Bucket"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Feed bag and bucket",body="The animal feed bag smells like pesticide, not grain. The bucket reeks of it too. Someone ran chemicals through the feed mill."},
{id="t0417-05",kind="set",pieces={"SeedBag","DuctTape"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="seed bag and duct tape",body="The seed bag has test markers and chemical residue inside. The duct tape holding it melted and corroded through. Found it in an experimental field plot."},
{id="t0417-06",kind="set",pieces={"EmptyJar","Map"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Empty jar and map",body="The empty jar has a label with grid numbers. The map shows the same grid in a field somewhere. They were running trials."},
{id="t0417-07",kind="set",pieces={"Bread","DishCloth"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Bread and dish cloth",body="The bread has a numbered tag pinned to it. I wiped the tape off with the dish cloth. It matches the tags on the closure notices."},
{id="t0417-08",kind="set",pieces={"Soap2","Sponge"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="soap and sponge",body="The soap and sponge hang from a guard's numbered tag. Tape on the shelf reads 'Zone 2, closed, do not enter'. A list beside them counts 14 names, all crossed off."},
{id="t0417-09",kind="set",pieces={"GardeningSprayEmpty","Postcard"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Postcard and empty sprayer",body="A postcard and an empty sprayer lie together. The card asks for supper to be kept warm. A ring from the sprayer smudges the ink."},
{id="t0417-10",kind="set",pieces={"Fertilizer","GlassTumbler"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Fertilizer and drinking glass",body="Fine grains cling to the rim of a drinking glass. The fertilizer sack beside it is sealed with household thread. A strip of cloth holds the pair together."},
-- T0418
{id="t0418-01",kind="set",pieces={"Map","Pencil"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Map and pencil",body="A road is rubbed out on this map. Six small figures are drawn beside it. The pencil has worn through the paper there. Someone waited, I think."},
{id="t0418-02",kind="set",pieces={"Clipboard","Eraser"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Clipboard and eraser",body="The clipboard lists four vehicle numbers and no names. Someone used the eraser on a fifth line. I can still feel a child's handwriting pressed into it."},
{id="t0418-03",kind="set",pieces={"FirstAidKit","BathTowel"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="First aid kit and towel",body="A sealed first aid kit is tied to a towel marked for a passenger. The seat is crossed off, but the towel is still damp."},
{id="t0418-04",kind="set",pieces={"Map","SheetPaper2"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Map and loose page",body="The loose page gives a different route from the map's inked one. Someone traced both with a stained finger. There is a hurried thumbprint on the corner."},
{id="t0418-05",kind="set",pieces={"HandTorch","Battery"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Torch and battery",body="The battery is taped to a torch beside a handwritten departure time. Looks like the owner waited long enough to use up the spare."},
{id="t0418-06",kind="set",pieces={"Badge","RubberBand"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Badge and rubber band",body="A badge and a band for counting arrivals are tied together. The band has an extra notch the badge doesn't show. A short tally was added after it was tied."},
{id="t0418-07",kind="set",pieces={"Jack","LugWrench"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Jack and lug wrench",body="The jack has fresh road grit and the wrench has warning tape. Looks like the repair was dropped beside a penciled clearance time."},
{id="t0418-08",kind="set",pieces={"WalkieTalkie1","Pencil"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Walkie-talkie and pencil",body="A frequency is scratched into the pencil's paint. The radio's own label names another channel. The paper around it says to wait."},
{id="t0418-09",kind="set",pieces={"Notebook","RedPen"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Notebook and red pen",body="A household count fills the notebook, six names to a page.\nA red pen squeezes one more in along the edge.\nThe line below for a pickup spot fades out half-written."},
{id="t0418-10",kind="set",pieces={"Bag_Schoolbag","Map"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Schoolbag and map",body="The bag holds an unused lunch wrapper. The map is folded to a stop crossed out twice. A child wrote a time on the strap, I think."},
-- T0419
{id="t0419-01",kind="set",pieces={"EmptyJar","SeedBag"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Empty jar and seed bag",body="Yellow grains crust the rim of the jar. They spill from a torn seed sack tied to it. The sack's label names a test plot."},
{id="t0419-02",kind="set",pieces={"WaterBottle","Bucket"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Water bottle and bucket",body="A clean bottle and a cloudy bucket share a chalk mark. I think the bucket was filled far from the rows, after the spraying."},
{id="t0419-03",kind="set",pieces={"Gloves_LeatherGloves","GardeningSprayEmpty"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Leather gloves and sprayer",body="One glove cuff holds field dust, the other kitchen soap. Looks like the empty sprayer was carried past a household door."},
{id="t0419-04",kind="set",pieces={"AnimalFeedBag","Bucket"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Feed bag and bucket",body="The feed sack has an oily streak beneath its fold. The pail has the same oily mark above the waterline. A few yellow grains float in it."},
{id="t0419-05",kind="set",pieces={"SeedBag","DuctTape"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Seed bag and duct tape",body="Tape seals a slit in the seed sack. Pale treated-seed dust has caught on the outside of the tape. A child's height is marked on it."},
{id="t0419-06",kind="set",pieces={"EmptyJar","Map"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Empty jar and map",body="The empty jar holds a folded list of 20 names. The map has roadblocks and checkpoints circled in pen. An order on the map says tell no one the route."},
{id="t0419-07",kind="set",pieces={"Bread","DishCloth"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Bread and dish cloth",body="The loaf is wrapped in clean cloth, the knot never opened. Barrier tape lies across the knot, with a numbered tag beneath. Someone retied the string after the morning patrol cleared the block."},
{id="t0419-08",kind="set",pieces={"Soap2","Sponge"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Soap and sponge",body="The sponge is dry and the soap is worn on one edge only. They are in a bag sealed with barrier tape, beside a small cup. A numbered tag is tied to the bag."},
{id="t0419-09",kind="set",pieces={"GardeningSprayEmpty","Postcard"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="postcard and empty sprayer",body="The postcard advertises a new crop treatment, free trial offer. The empty sprayer rests on it, nozzle caked with residue. Someone applied the entire concentrate to one field."},
{id="t0419-10",kind="set",pieces={"Fertilizer","GlassTumbler"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Fertilizer and drinking glass",body="The fertilizer and glass are bound with barrier tape. An evacuation tag dangles from them, thumbprint and partial stamp. Seal's intact, so they logged it, but nobody came back."},
-- T0420
{id="t0420-01",kind="written",pieces={"diary"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Diary page",body="They told us the road was still open. The map pinned beside the shopping list had already been changed in pencil, and the neighbor who came for water said the gate was locked.\n\nI kept the older copy in a coat pocket while everyone else was told to use the new one. I had meant to save it only until someone could explain the difference. By then the ordinary work around us had stopped."},
{id="t0420-02",kind="written",pieces={"notebook"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Notebook page",body="I counted everyone in the queue before I counted cars. The person carrying the list wrote down the cars first and ran out of room for the family walking behind them.\n\nThe youngest still asked whether the driver knew where we were. We compared what we had seen with what was written there. The second account omitted the small part that had frightened us."},
{id="t0420-03",kind="written",pieces={"letter"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Letter",body="My brother stayed for the later vehicle because our aunt could not get into the first. Its time was written on the back of a lunch receipt. No driver at the next barrier knew of it.\n\nThe pencil count did not change when the people standing beside me did. I left the date on the page and did not try to straighten the damaged edge. Someone else might remember the same afternoon."},
{id="t0420-04",kind="written",pieces={"notepad"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Notepad page",body="The house was marked cleared while we were still packing. I put a square around the date on our own copy. We waited for someone to return and ask who was inside.\n\nThe person who had written the first directions could no longer be found. My family asked me to put the paper away with the bills. I kept it separate because the person involved might come back for it."},
{id="t0420-05",kind="written",pieces={"diary"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Diary page",body="The woman at the gate read our names aloud and put us on a bus list. Another person came out with a new list and said the first bus had already taken us.\n\nI left room for a correction and carried the paper through the night. I had meant to save it only until someone could explain the difference. By then the ordinary work around us had stopped."},
{id="t0420-06",kind="written",pieces={"notebook"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Notebook page",body="A man in a vest promised to come back after he moved the first group. His pencil left an unfinished arrow on my paper. I kept the page when the rest of the notices were pulled down.\n\nThe last vehicle passed with space for the supplies but none listed for us. We compared what we had seen with what was written there. The second account omitted the small part that had frightened us."},
{id="t0420-07",kind="written",pieces={"letter"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Letter",body="We followed the directions given at dawn and found a chain across the road. Someone had moved the crossing but left the old sign standing. My father had memorized its distance because he could not read the smaller print.\n\nI kept the older copy in a coat pocket while everyone else was told to use the new one. I left the date on the page and did not try to straighten the damaged edge. Someone else might remember the same afternoon."},
{id="t0420-08",kind="written",pieces={"notepad"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Notepad page",body="The clerk counted the beds as if each held one person. My mother was sitting beside my sister, waiting for her to stand. On the posted total there was only one of them.\n\nThe youngest still asked whether the driver knew where we were. My family asked me to put the paper away with the bills. I kept it separate because the person involved might come back for it."},
{id="t0420-09",kind="written",pieces={"diary"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Diary page",body="I sent a change of address with the driver who said he could cross. The parcel came back with the new address rubbed out. The note from my husband inside had never been opened.\n\nThe pencil count did not change when the people standing beside me did. I had meant to save it only until someone could explain the difference. By then the ordinary work around us had stopped."},
{id="t0420-10",kind="written",pieces={"notebook"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Notebook page",body="I copied the first line because it included our street. The replacement left the street out but retained the same number of vehicles. We stood beside the mailbox until the engines were gone.\n\nThe person who had written the first directions could no longer be found. We compared what we had seen with what was written there. The second account omitted the small part that had frightened us."},
-- T0421
{id="t0421-01",kind="written",pieces={"diary"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Diary page",body="The bottle looked clean until it dried, when a green line appeared above the water. We had filled it from the tap after the field truck sprayed the far rows, the ones with the new seed mix.\n\nThe dog would not drink from the dish left outside. I kept the bottle until someone could tell me what was in that spray."},
{id="t0421-02",kind="written",pieces={"notebook"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Garden notes",body="The new pesticide rig came through early morning. Even my covered herbs were wilting by evening.\n\nYellow residue coated the car and laundry on the line. I pressed this leaf to see if the next row would go the same way."},
{id="t0421-03",kind="written",pieces={"letter"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Treatment Record",body="The treated seed arrived with double concentration markings. Driver said it was meant for commercial spray equipment. We stored the sacks near the rain barrel overnight.\n\nChemical residue washed into our water during the storm. Everything watered from the barrel yellowed within days. The dilution ratio printed was for industrial use only."},
{id="t0421-04",kind="written",pieces={"notepad"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Field notes",body="The workers marked the trial acres with stakes that morning. By afternoon the pale dust had settled on our garden rows. I watched them spray only the test section but both fields wilted.\n\nThe boundary stakes did not contain it."},
{id="t0421-05",kind="written",pieces={"diary"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Diary page",body="I was asked to keep this sample apart from the cooking jars. Its lid came loose on the way back from the orchard. The grocery bag was set on the table before I noticed the sweet chemical smell.\n\nThe child's blanket was drying nearby and held the same fine dust. The potted peppers on the sill curled the next morning. I had meant to save it only until someone could explain the difference."},
{id="t0421-06",kind="written",pieces={"notebook"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Notebook page",body="They taped off the boundary posts after the checkpoint went up. The path we knew to the outer road now lies beyond the last post. We had walked it that morning with the children, before a patrol turned us back and noted down our names.\n\nWe were told not to use the path again and to say nothing if questioned. I folded this page small and put it away from the others."},
{id="t0421-07",kind="written",pieces={"letter"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Letter",body="The calves refused their water before the county car appeared. I poured it into a spare pail and found an oily rim when it settled. We had drawn it from the same shallow well as ours.\n\nThe dog would no longer drink from the dish left outside. I left the date on the page and did not try to straighten the damaged edge. Someone else might remember the same afternoon."},
{id="t0421-08",kind="written",pieces={"notepad"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Notepad page",body="The driver washed the sprayer beside the feed shop. He paid for soap but not for another bucket. The rinse water ran through the drain toward gardens downhill, and the beds there showed bleached leaf edges by the weekend.\n\nI kept the paper separate from the bills because the person involved might come back for it."},
{id="t0421-09",kind="written",pieces={"diary"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Diary page",body="The first rain after the field treatment left yellow flecks in a pan under the leak. We had shut the window before the truck came. I saved the pan because no one believed me when I described it.\n\nThe next family along the road noticed the smell without seeing the truck. I had meant to save it only until someone could explain the difference. By then the ordinary work around us had stopped."},
{id="t0421-10",kind="written",pieces={"notebook"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Order receipt",body="The receipt includes a charge for trial pesticide in sample jars. A household address is written beside it, not a field number. The concentration marked is higher than on the field containers. Reapplication was scheduled three days after the first delivery."},
-- T0422
