{id="t0425-01",kind="written",pieces={"diary"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Diary page",body="The bottle looked clean until it dried, when a green line appeared above the water. We had filled it after the field truck passed, at a tap on the other side of the road.\n\nThe child’s blanket was drying nearby and held the same fine dust. I left the date on the page and did not try to straighten the damaged edge. Someone else might remember the same afternoon."},
{id="t0425-02",kind="written",pieces={"notebook"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Notebook page",body="I covered the herbs when the trial vehicle passed. By evening the leaves under the cover had curled too. The neighbor said the spray could not have crossed the fence, but her laundry had the same pale grains.\n\nWe washed the small cup twice and put it away from the others. My family asked me to put the paper away with the bills. I kept it separate because the person involved might come back for it."},
{id="t0425-03",kind="written",pieces={"letter"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Letter",body="The feed-store driver left a sack of the new treated grain and washed his hands before accepting a cup of tea. He said the sack dust burned. The delivery slip said nothing of it.\n\nThe dog would not drink from the dish left outside. The barley I sowed from that sack came up thin and spotted, row after row."},
{id="t0425-04",kind="written",pieces={"notepad"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Notepad page",body="The workers took their boots off outside after the spraying. By morning the pale dust had still traveled inside on the dog's paws. No one in the house had gone near the sprayed rows.\n\nThe lettuce bed by the door has gone limp where the dog crossed it. I set the page beside the boots."},
{id="t0425-05",kind="written",pieces={"diary"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Sample jar lid",body="The new spray came with test strips to check orchard runoff. I kept one jar on the porch to compare with the treated rows. The lid seal failed overnight and the smell reached the next farm."},
{id="t0425-06",kind="written",pieces={"notebook"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Notebook page",body="We sprayed the lower field after the seed trial. The water path runs beside it, and the wind carried the mist across. The squash along that path has blackened leaves in a long streak.\n\nI wrote down the day because the leaves turned afterward. I kept the page separate from the bills."},
{id="t0425-07",kind="written",pieces={"letter"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Letter",body="The calves refused their water before the county car appeared. I poured it into a spare pail and found an oily rim when it settled. We had drawn it from the same shallow well as ours.\n\nThe child’s blanket was drying nearby and held the same fine dust. I had meant to save it only until someone could explain the difference. By then the ordinary work around us had stopped."},
{id="t0425-08",kind="written",pieces={"notepad"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Notepad page",body="The driver washed the spray rig beside the feed shop. The rinse ran down the drain toward the vegetable plots behind the houses, and by the next week the cabbages there had yellowed in a fan shape.\n\nWe washed the small cup twice and put it away from the others. I noted the cabbage rows on the page."},
{id="t0425-09",kind="written",pieces={"diary"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Diary page",body="The first rain after the field treatment left yellow flecks in a pan under the leak. The same flecks sit on the wheat leaves, thick along the rows we sprayed and absent where we did not.\n\nThe dog would not drink from the dish left outside. I saved the pan because no one believed me when I described it."},
{id="t0425-10",kind="written",pieces={"notebook"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Notebook page",body="The seed counter receipt lists a small charge for sample jars and a sack of the new treated seed. The shopkeeper wrote a field number beside it. The corn from that sack came up grey-streaked and stunted.\n\nI kept the receipt with my planting notes so I could compare the rows."},
-- T0426
{id="t0426-01",kind="written",pieces={"diary"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Diary page",body="They told us the road was still open. The map pinned beside the shopping list had already been changed in pencil, and the neighbor who came for water said the gate was locked.\n\nI kept the older copy in a coat pocket while everyone else was told to use the new one. My family asked me to put the paper away with the bills. I kept it separate because the person involved might come back for it."},
{id="t0426-02",kind="written",pieces={"notebook"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Notebook page",body="I counted everyone in the queue before I counted cars. The person carrying the list wrote down the cars first and ran out of room for the family walking behind them.\n\nThe youngest still asked whether the driver knew where we were. I had meant to save it only until someone could explain the difference. By then the ordinary work around us had stopped."},
{id="t0426-03",kind="written",pieces={"letter"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Letter",body="My brother stayed for the later vehicle because our aunt could not get into the first. Its time was written on the back of a lunch receipt. No driver at the next barrier knew of it.\n\nThe pencil count did not change when the people standing beside me did. We compared what we had seen with what was written there. The second account omitted the small part that had frightened us."},
{id="t0426-04",kind="written",pieces={"notepad"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Notepad page",body="The house was marked cleared while we were still packing. I put a square around the date on our own copy. We waited for someone to return and ask who was inside.\n\nThe person who had written the first directions could no longer be found. I left the date on the page and did not try to straighten the damaged edge. Someone else might remember the same afternoon."},
{id="t0426-05",kind="written",pieces={"diary"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Diary page",body="The woman at the gate read our names aloud and put us on a bus list. Another person came out with a new list and said the first bus had already taken us.\n\nI left room for a correction and carried the paper through the night. My family asked me to put the paper away with the bills. I kept it separate because the person involved might come back for it."},
{id="t0426-06",kind="written",pieces={"notebook"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Notebook page",body="A man in a vest promised to come back after he moved the first group. His pencil left an unfinished arrow on my paper. I kept the page when the rest of the notices were pulled down.\n\nThe last vehicle passed with space for the supplies but none listed for us. I had meant to save it only until someone could explain the difference. By then the ordinary work around us had stopped."},
{id="t0426-07",kind="written",pieces={"letter"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Letter",body="We followed the directions given at dawn and found a chain across the road. Someone had moved the crossing but left the old sign standing. My father had memorized its distance because he could not read the smaller print.\n\nI kept the older copy in a coat pocket while everyone else was told to use the new one. We compared what we had seen with what was written there. The second account omitted the small part that had frightened us."},
{id="t0426-08",kind="written",pieces={"notepad"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Notepad page",body="The clerk counted the beds as if each held one person. My mother was sitting beside my sister, waiting for her to stand. On the posted total there was only one of them.\n\nThe youngest still asked whether the driver knew where we were. I left the date on the page and did not try to straighten the damaged edge. Someone else might remember the same afternoon."},
{id="t0426-09",kind="written",pieces={"diary"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Diary page",body="I sent a change of address with the driver who said he could cross. The parcel came back with the new address rubbed out. The note from my husband inside had never been opened.\n\nThe pencil count did not change when the people standing beside me did. My family asked me to put the paper away with the bills. I kept it separate because the person involved might come back for it."},
{id="t0426-10",kind="written",pieces={"notebook"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Notebook page",body="I copied the first line because it included our street. The replacement left the street out but retained the same number of vehicles. We stood beside the mailbox until the engines were gone.\n\nThe person who had written the first directions could no longer be found. I had meant to save it only until someone could explain the difference. By then the ordinary work around us had stopped."},
-- T0427
{id="t0427-01",kind="written",pieces={"diary"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Diary page",body="The bottle looked clean until it dried, when a green line appeared above the water. We had filled it at a tap beside the sprayed field, and the same green line rings the sprayer tank.\n\nThe dog would not drink from the dish left outside. The turnip tops by that tap have gone limp."},
{id="t0427-02",kind="written",pieces={"notebook"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Garden notes",body="I covered the herbs when the trial vehicle passed. By evening the leaves under the cover had curled too. The neighbor said the spray could not cross the fence. Her wash and my car both showed the pale dust."},
{id="t0427-03",kind="written",pieces={"letter"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Letter",body="A driver came to the gate with a list of households and stopped to accept a cup of tea. He asked us not to use the back road, which was closed by a barrier.\n\nThe list had a number beside our name and he would not say what it counted. Everyone on the road was told to keep quiet about it."},
{id="t0427-04",kind="written",pieces={"notepad"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Notepad page",body="The workers removed their boots outside. By morning the pale dust had traveled inside on the dog’s paws. No one in the house had gone near the trial rows.\n\nI wrote down the day because the first warning arrived after it. I left the date on the page and did not try to straighten the damaged edge. Someone else might remember the same afternoon."},
{id="t0427-05",kind="written",pieces={"diary"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Diary page",body="I was asked to keep this sample apart from the cooking jars. Its lid came loose on the way back from the orchard. The grocery bag was set on the table before I noticed the smell.\n\nThe child’s blanket was drying nearby and held the same fine dust. My family asked me to put the paper away with the bills. I kept it separate because the person involved might come back for it."},
{id="t0427-06",kind="written",pieces={"notebook"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Notebook page",body="We sprayed the lower field after the seed trial. The water path runs beside it, and the mist drifted over the rows we had walked that morning. The tomato vines there are spotted and curling.\n\nWe washed the small cup twice and put it away from the others. I kept this page to compare with next season's rows."},
{id="t0427-07",kind="written",pieces={"letter"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Letter",body="The calves refused their water. I poured it into a spare pail and found an oily rim once it settled, the same sheen as the puddles in the sprayed pasture. We draw from the same shallow well as the field.\n\nThe dog would not drink either. The rye along that pasture has gone patchy and pale."},
{id="t0427-08",kind="written",pieces={"notepad"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Notepad page",body="The driver washed the spray rig beside the feed shop. The rinse ran down the drain toward the vegetable plots behind the houses, and the beans there blistered and dropped their flowers within the week.\n\nI left the date on the page and did not smooth the torn edge. I kept notes on which rows were hit."},
{id="t0427-09",kind="written",pieces={"diary"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Diary page",body="The first rain after the field treatment left yellow flecks in a pan under the leak. We had shut the window before the truck came. I saved the pan because no one believed me when I described it.\n\nThe next family along the road noticed the smell without seeing the truck. My family asked me to put the paper away with the bills. I kept it separate because the person involved might come back for it."},
{id="t0427-10",kind="written",pieces={"notebook"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Notebook page",body="The seed counter receipt lists a small charge for sample jars and a sack of the new treated seed. The shopkeeper wrote a field number beside it. The corn from that sack came up grey-streaked and stunted.\n\nI wrote down the planting day beside the receipt so I could compare the rows after the rain."},
-- T0428
{id="t0428-01",kind="set",pieces={"SeedBag","Fertilizer"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Seed bag and fertilizer",body="This seam has two colors of dust. The fertilizer reached the lower half. The dry seed at the top still looks clean to me."},
{id="t0428-02",kind="set",pieces={"HandShovel","Bucket"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="vehicle",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Hand shovel and bucket",body="The soil on this shovel stops at a sharp pale band. Above it the blade is crusted with spray residue and field grit. The bucket holds stunted seedlings."},
{id="t0428-03",kind="set",pieces={"CornSeed","Twine"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Corn seed and twine",body="Someone used twine to mark these corn seeds apart. Half are darker, almost rotted. The other half look ready to plant again."},
{id="t0428-04",kind="set",pieces={"SeedBag","Rope"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Seed bag and rope",body="A folded seed bag with loose feed at the bottom, tied by a rope. The rope also holds a strip of another bag with spray stains. The leaves nearby look sick and spotted."},
{id="t0428-05",kind="set",pieces={"EmptyJar","WaterBottle"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Empty jar and water bottle",body="The jar is taped shut with a numbered strip. The water bottle beside it has an identical strip. I think they were counted at a checkpoint and left."},
{id="t0428-06",kind="set",pieces={"SeedBag","CompostBag"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Seed bag and compost bag",body="The lowest sack has sprouted through its stitches. The bag above it is dry and still sealed."},
{id="t0428-07",kind="set",pieces={"Gloves_Dish","CarrotSeed"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="corpse",lean="agricultural",rival="containment",outfit="farm"}},title="Dish gloves and carrot seed",body="A garden glove is folded around a seed packet. The fingertips have a dark crust. The packet's paper doesn't."},
{id="t0428-08",kind="set",pieces={"Tarp","HandShovel"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Tarp and hand shovel",body="Seedlings under the tarp stayed green. The shovel's from when I planted more - those went black by morning."},
{id="t0428-09",kind="set",pieces={"CornSeed","Pot"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Corn seed and pot",body="This corn seed never got planted, still sitting in the pot. The others all went in during treatment week. Only these two made it through whatever happened out there."},
{id="t0428-10",kind="set",pieces={"Bowl","Fork","SeedBag"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="vehicle",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Bowl, fork and seed bag",body="There is fresh soil in the lunch bowl and none on the fork. Someone set food down to carry a wet seed bag back in."},
-- T0429
{id="t0429-01",kind="set",pieces={"Bucket","Bowl"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="bucket and bowl",body="The bucket has a closure notice taped inside the rim. The bowl holds a list of names, half of them struck out."},
{id="t0429-02",kind="set",pieces={"WaterBottle","Twine"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Water bottle and twine",body="Two water bottles are tied together with twine. Each has a numbered tag and a strip of tape. A patrol must have left them as a marker."},
{id="t0429-03",kind="set",pieces={"Kettle","Bucket","Tarp"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Kettle, bucket and tarp",body="A tarp covers a kettle and a bucket stacked together. Tape says do not move, closed by order until cleared. A checkpoint number is written on the kettle."},
{id="t0429-04",kind="set",pieces={"Bowl","Bucket","WaterBottle"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Bowl, bucket and water bottle",body="The untouched bowl has the same green ring as the sprayer can. The overturned water bottle near it is clear. A wilted seedling lies across the bucket rim."},
{id="t0429-05",kind="set",pieces={"FishingNet","Bucket"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="vehicle",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Fishing net and bucket",body="My fishing net caught pale spray granules where the runoff narrowed. The bucket of dry mud from above the waterline has none. Dead fish lay where the crop rows end."},
{id="t0429-06",kind="set",pieces={"EmptyJar","JarLid"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Empty jar and jar lid",body="The empty jar and the jar lid both carry a guard's numbered tape. A list taped to the shelf shows 12 names, all crossed off. An order says nobody opens or mentions them."},
{id="t0429-07",kind="set",pieces={"RubberHose","Wrench","Fertilizer"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="vehicle",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Rubber hose, wrench and fertilizer",body="The rubber hose still smells like well water. A wrench lies near it, handle stained greenish. The fertilizer bag is torn open and empty."},
{id="t0429-08",kind="set",pieces={"Bucket","Spoon"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Bucket and spoon",body="A spoon hangs from the bucket by a tagged string. The tag lists a count of people and a closure date. The count is written over twice."},
{id="t0429-09",kind="set",pieces={"Shoes_WorkBoots","Bucket"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Work boots and bucket",body="The boot has spray residue caked in its tread. A bucket of gray rinse water is beside it. The seedlings in it have yellowed, and the other boot is clean."},
{id="t0429-10",kind="set",pieces={"Wrench","Bucket"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Wrench and bucket",body="The wrench has a numbered tag wired to the handle. A bucket beyond it holds a sheet of orders to stay silent."},
-- T0430
{id="t0430-01",kind="set",pieces={"SeedBag","Rope"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Seed bag and rope",body="The seed bag is open, rope looped through the top eyelets. Seeds spilled across the ground but nothing's touched them. Not even ants."},
{id="t0430-02",kind="set",pieces={"Milk","Spoon"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Milk and spoon",body="The milk carton has a tape strip across the cap. A spoon taped to it carries a number. A note says nobody is to open them before the count."},
{id="t0430-03",kind="set",pieces={"Egg","CornSeed"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Egg and corn seed",body="The egg smells wrong, sort of chemical. The corn seed nearby has a waxy green coating on it. They were both right at the coop door."},
{id="t0430-04",kind="set",pieces={"Bucket","Wire"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Bucket and wire",body="Wire runs along the fence posts to a checkpoint gate. The bucket hung on it holds numbered tags. A patrol seems to have counted each post."},
{id="t0430-05",kind="set",pieces={"FishingNet","SeedBag"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Fishing net and seed bag",body="The fishing net holds a torn seed bag inside. Seeds touching the mesh turned gray and brittle. The ones that didn't touch stayed normal yellow. Someone hung this up as a bird feeder."},
{id="t0430-06",kind="set",pieces={"Rope","Bowl"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Rope and bowl",body="The rope is knotted at intervals, each knot with a tag. The bowl at one end holds a list of numbers. I think it marked a line people were told not to cross."},
{id="t0430-07",kind="set",pieces={"Apple","Corn"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Apple and corn",body="Two apples are bruised but clean. The corn in the same crate has a powder along its seam. I don't see it on the fruit."},
{id="t0430-08",kind="set",pieces={"Broom","SeedBag"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Broom and seed bag",body="The broom has dark grain caught in its bristles. The swept pile was bagged apart from the clean straw."},
{id="t0430-09",kind="set",pieces={"Spoon","Twine","Corn"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="vehicle",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Spoon, twine and corn",body="The spoon still has corn dust in the bowl. Twine wrapped tight around the handle, like someone marked it. I've seen what happens to people who worked those fields."},
{id="t0430-10",kind="set",pieces={"Bowl","Rope","CornSeed"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Bowl, rope and corn seed",body="The bowl has a dark residue dried to the bottom. Same stuff crusted on the rope they used for the sprayer. The corn seed in the bag turned grey after that week."},
-- T0431
{id="t0431-01",kind="set",pieces={"TirePump","Tarp"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="vehicle",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Tire pump and tarp",body="A tire pump is wrapped in a tarp and tagged with a number. Tape on the tarp reads held for inspection. I think a patrol took the car and left this."},
{id="t0431-02",kind="set",pieces={"Shovel","Bucket"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="vehicle",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Shovel and bucket",body="This shovel carries two soils. There's red clay under a fresh layer of pale spray dust. The bucket holds only the pale dust and a few yellowed seedlings."},
{id="t0431-03",kind="set",pieces={"Shovel","Fertilizer"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="vehicle",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Shovel and fertilizer",body="This shovel's been in the fertilizer. The handle has paint from another barn."},
{id="t0431-04",kind="set",pieces={"DuctTape","RubberHose","WaterBottle"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="vehicle",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Duct tape, hose and water bottle",body="The duct tape holds a split spray hose together. Its inner edge is green. The water bottle beneath the patch is flecked the same way."},
{id="t0431-05",kind="set",pieces={"Tarp","Rope"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="vehicle",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="tarp and rope",body="The tarp is stiff with dried yellow residue that flakes at touch. Rope coiled nearby shows the same yellow coating on every fiber. Both carry a sharp chemical smell."},
{id="t0431-06",kind="set",pieces={"SeedBag","Tarp"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="vehicle",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Seed bag and tarp",body="The seed bag is ripped open. Black dust coats the tarp underneath. Same dust I saw on those dead crops last week."},
{id="t0431-07",kind="set",pieces={"Broom","Twine"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="vehicle",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Broom and twine",body="Someone tied this broom to a gate post with twine. A tag on the twine lists times of patrol passes. The last time is a day after the closure."},
{id="t0431-08",kind="set",pieces={"RubberHose","Bucket"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="vehicle",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Rubber hose and bucket",body="The bucket's full of green chemical residue, still wet. The rubber hose drips concentrate onto withered leaves below. Someone left it running."},
{id="t0431-09",kind="set",pieces={"Rope","SeedBag"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="vehicle",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Rope and seed bag",body="The rope has chemical burns where it touched the seed bag. Both reek of something harsh. This got hauled from the field to town."},
{id="t0431-10",kind="set",pieces={"HandShovel","WaterBottle"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="vehicle",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Hand shovel and water bottle",body="The spade blade was rinsed. Green soil is left in the socket where the water couldn't reach."},
-- T0432
{id="t0432-01",kind="set",pieces={"Bread","WaterBottle","Tissue"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="corpse",lean="agricultural",rival="containment",outfit="farm"}},title="bread, water bottle and tissue",body="The bread sits dry but pale powder lines the water bottle. A tissue shows the same dust. The sprayer rig still sits in the adjacent row."},
{id="t0432-02",kind="set",pieces={"Shoes_WorkBoots","Newspaper"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="corpse",lean="containment",rival="agricultural",outfit="farm"}},title="Work boots and newspaper",body="One work boot is stuffed with newspaper from the closure day. A numbered tag is laced to the other boot. The tag matches a list I saw at the checkpoint."},
{id="t0432-03",kind="set",pieces={"RippedSheets","Fertilizer"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="corpse",lean="agricultural",rival="containment",outfit="farm"}},title="Ripped sheets and fertilizer",body="There are fresh drops on this cloth over a smear of fertilizer dust. The dry cloth tied beside it has none."},
{id="t0432-04",kind="set",pieces={"Bowl","Bread"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="vehicle",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Bowl and bread",body="A lunch bowl has grain husks stuck to its rim. The unopened bread beside it looks packed for the same shift."},
{id="t0432-05",kind="set",pieces={"Jacket_ArmyCamoGreen","WaterBottle"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="corpse",lean="agricultural",rival="containment",outfit="farm"}},title="Camo jacket and water bottle",body="Dark treated-feed dust covers the outer sleeve of this jacket. A bottle inside has the same residue at its neck. A scorched crop leaf is in a pocket."},
{id="t0432-06",kind="set",pieces={"WaterBottle","RippedSheets"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="corpse",lean="agricultural",rival="containment",outfit="farm"}},title="Water bottle and ripped sheets",body="A full bottle is knotted to a cloth strip with a brown stain. A scorched leaf of seed corn lies beside it. The cloth has a dusting of sprayed powder."},
{id="t0432-07",kind="set",pieces={"HandShovel","Bandage"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="corpse",lean="agricultural",rival="containment",outfit="farm"}},title="Hand shovel and bandage",body="The hand shovel has fresh field soil. A cloth on its grip is stained green from the sprayer. A bandage was laid out but never used."},
{id="t0432-08",kind="set",pieces={"Purse","Spoon"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="corpse",lean="containment",rival="agricultural",outfit="farm"}},title="Purse and spoon",body="A numbered tag is clipped inside this purse. The spoon beside it has tape marked with a count. I think they were taken at a checkpoint and dropped."},
{id="t0432-09",kind="set",pieces={"Jacket_ArmyOliveDrab","Tissue"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="corpse",lean="agricultural",rival="containment",outfit="farm"}},title="olive jacket and tissue",body="The olive jacket reeks of pesticide. White residue stains both cuffs and collar. Crushed crop leaves cling to the fabric. The tissue in the pocket is still folded."},
{id="t0432-10",kind="set",pieces={"Soap2","Gloves_Dish","WaterBottle"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="corpse",lean="containment",rival="agricultural",outfit="farm"}},title="soap, dish gloves and bottle",body="The soap, dish gloves and water bottle share patrol tag 31. Tape on the bottle reads 'Hold for the convoy'. The tag orders everyone to tell no one where it was found."},
-- T0433
{id="t0433-01",kind="set",pieces={"SeedBag","Newspaper"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="mailbox",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Seed bag and newspaper",body="A seed packet leaked into this mailbox. The paper at the bottom is gritty. The letters above it stayed clean."},
{id="t0433-02",kind="set",pieces={"CornSeed","SeedBag"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="mailbox",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Corn seed and seed bag",body="The opened packet is bound with a rubber band. A few dark kernels remain. A second unopened packet is tucked behind it."},
{id="t0433-03",kind="set",pieces={"SeedBag","Spoon"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="mailbox",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Seed bag and spoon",body="A seed bag strip and a spoon were pushed in here together. The spoon still has the same dark grains stuck to the strip."},
{id="t0433-04",kind="set",pieces={"CarrotSeed","CornSeed"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="mailbox",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Carrot seed and corn seed",body="These seeds came back with blackened tips. The packet mailed out beside them is still sealed."},
{id="t0433-05",kind="set",pieces={"Map","Twine","Corn"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="mailbox",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Map, twine and corn",body="Corn tied to the map with twine. Two circles in pencil, one crossed. The twine still smells like field chemicals."},
{id="t0433-06",kind="set",pieces={"EmptyJar","CarrotSeed"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="mailbox",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Empty jar and seed",body="I found an empty jar with green residue caked inside. A carrot seed packet is taped across the top. It was stored in the chemical shed behind the barn."},
{id="t0433-07",kind="set",pieces={"Newspaper","Tomato"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="mailbox",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Newspaper and tomato",body="A newspaper is wrapped around a withered tomato vine. Its leaves are freckled where field dust collected."},
{id="t0433-08",kind="set",pieces={"DuctTape","SeedBag"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="mailbox",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Duct tape and seed bag",body="Duct tape stuck to the seed bag corner. Two arrows drawn on it pointed somewhere else. Someone was tracking something through the fields."},
{id="t0433-09",kind="set",pieces={"SeedBag","Rope"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="mailbox",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Seed bag and rope",body="The seed bag is tied shut with rope. The knot looks professional. Dark residue stains the outside. Nothing grew where it spilled."},
{id="t0433-10",kind="set",pieces={"CornSeed","EmptyJar"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="mailbox",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Corn seed and empty jar",body="One corn seed packet is damp and swollen. Another was packed dry beside it, next to an empty jar. Someone left both here for collection."},
-- T0434
{id="t0434-01",kind="set",pieces={"Tarp","Cabbage"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Tarp and cabbage",body="Under this tarp the cabbage stayed fresh. Past the edge, every head has those brown spots."},
{id="t0434-02",kind="set",pieces={"EmptyJar","HandShovel"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Empty jar and hand shovel",body="The empty jar held brown soil from the fields. Gray dirt cakes the hand shovel now. All the roots died."},
{id="t0434-03",kind="set",pieces={"SeedBag","Pencil"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Seed bag and pencil",body="This seed bag and pencil were marked for late sowing. Those beds are still green. The earlier ones collapsed."},
{id="t0434-04",kind="set",pieces={"Newspaper","Potato"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="newspaper potatoes",body="Newspaper kept some safe. Field potatoes all rotted. Happened overnight. Strange residue on the dark ones."},
{id="t0434-05",kind="set",pieces={"Bucket","Tarp"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Bucket and tarp",body="Patrol tag 9 hangs from the bucket. Orders on the tarp read 'Road closed, turn back'. A checkpoint list on the tarp counts 40 people."},
{id="t0434-06",kind="set",pieces={"Twine","Fertilizer"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Twine and fertilizer",body="The twine here is caked in dried fertilizer. One side's crusted thick, facing the field. Someone left this during spraying season."},
{id="t0434-07",kind="set",pieces={"Potato","SeedBag"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Potatoes and seed bag",body="The potato under the seed bag is firm and clean. The ones from the rows all have soft spots now. Timing mattered here."},
{id="t0434-08",kind="set",pieces={"RippedSheets","Rope"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Torn sheets and rope",body="The cloth hung indoors is tied with numbered tape. The rope is cut where a patrol sign hung. I counted three tags on it and none were mine."},
{id="t0434-09",kind="set",pieces={"Kettle","Bowl","HandShovel"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Kettle, bowl and hand shovel",body="The water in this kettle is clear. A dish left in the yard has pale flecks like the soil in the shovel."},
{id="t0434-10",kind="set",pieces={"HandShovel","CarrotSeed"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Hand shovel and carrot seed",body="The shovel is brown on one edge and gray on the other. The gray soil holds dead seedlings. The brown side has live roots."},
-- T0435
{id="t0435-01",kind="set",pieces={"Map","SeedBag","Pencil"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="vehicle",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Map, seed bag and pencil",body="The vehicle map has pencil ticks at three stops. Dark grain in its fold looks like that in the half empty bag."},
{id="t0435-02",kind="set",pieces={"Bucket","Soap2","Gloves_Dish"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="vehicle",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Bucket, soap and dish gloves",body="The bucket, soap and dish gloves share patrol tag 18. Tape on the bucket reads 'Hold for the convoy'. I think the guards ordered everyone to leave them."},
{id="t0435-03",kind="set",pieces={"Map","CarrotSeed"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="vehicle",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Map and carrot seed",body="This map bends along the farm road. The carrot seed in the crease is black and split. I avoided the fields."},
{id="t0435-04",kind="set",pieces={"Tarp","SeedBag"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="vehicle",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Tarp and seed bag",body="The tarp has a clean rectangle where a crate stood. The seed bag beside it is dusted with the same pale powder. Maybe the load spilled before the crate was taken."},
{id="t0435-05",kind="set",pieces={"Spoon","Newspaper"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="vehicle",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Spoon wrapped in newspaper",body="The spoon is wrapped in newspaper from the day of the order. The paper lists road closures in a numbered column. Someone circled the closures nearest this stop."},
{id="t0435-06",kind="set",pieces={"Rope","SeedBag"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="vehicle",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Rope and seed bags",body="A knotted rope divides the bags. The sack on one side has a green dust mark. The ones on the other side are clean."},
{id="t0435-07",kind="set",pieces={"WaterBottle","Map"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="vehicle",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Water bottle and map",body="A water bottle sits on the map where two roads meet. The map has a checkpoint mark in tape at that spot. A patrol schedule is penciled in the margin."},
{id="t0435-08",kind="set",pieces={"Shovel","Tarp"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="vehicle",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Shovel and tarp",body="The shovel's handle has two different colored clays. The tarp wrapped around it has fresh tears. They look shaped by a narrow truck bed."},
{id="t0435-09",kind="set",pieces={"Pot","Fork"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="vehicle",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Pot and fork",body="A lunch pot is packed with a stack of numbered tags. The fork inside is taped to a list of names. Half the names are crossed out in the same hand."},
{id="t0435-10",kind="set",pieces={"TirePump","SeedBag"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="vehicle",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Tire pump and seed bag",body="This tire pump is streaked with pale dust. The seed bag has it too. Both were handled together before."},
-- T0436
{id="t0436-01",kind="written",pieces={"diary"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Diary entry",body="The calf stopped drinking after we opened the new feed. Its sister stayed in the back pen on the old sack and still pushed me for breakfast.\n\nI wrote that down before anyone thought to count people. The feed bill was due Friday. I kept telling myself the animal was sulking because I was late."},
{id="t0436-02",kind="written",pieces={"notepad"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Notepad page",body="We filled the near trough from the field line and the far one from the well. By dusk the near pen was quiet; the far pen made its usual racket.\n\nI switched the hose myself. My mother asked why I kept a note about water when the cattle needed hay."},
{id="t0436-03",kind="written",pieces={"notebook"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Notebook page",body="The bale under the roof was sound. The loose hay left beside the sprayer curled at the edges, and the rabbits would only eat from the roofed bale.\n\nI had promised to sweep both piles before supper. Now the clean one is marked with my old blue string so I can find it in a hurry."},
{id="t0436-04",kind="written",pieces={"diary"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Diary entry",body="My brother took the sacks to the poultry shed on Tuesday. He came back nauseated and slept through Wednesday's milking. The children who stayed in town were well that night.\n\nThe invoice sat under the sugar bowl because we still owed for the load. I was angry about the money before I was frightened about him."},
{id="t0436-05",kind="written",pieces={"letter"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="mailbox",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Letter",body="Our goats grazed the ditch after the field truck passed. The ones shut in the upper pen ate the same hay but never reached the ditch, and they kept their appetites.\n\nI used to complain that the upper gate stuck. That day I was grateful and ashamed of how long it took me to notice why."},
{id="t0436-06",kind="written",pieces={"notepad"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Notepad page",body="Only the flock beside the new grain bin stopped laying. I gave the birds in the yard from the old tin; they made noise all morning and left eggs by noon.\n\nI put the feed scoop on a shelf rather than wash it. It seemed useful to know exactly which bin it had touched."},
{id="t0436-07",kind="written",pieces={"diary"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Diary entry",body="I swept the packing room while the new seed bags were stacked there. By evening my throat burned. My cousin swept the empty stall next door and went to the dance.\n\nWe both laughed at my cough at first. I can still see the pale stripe the sacks left on the floor."},
{id="t0436-08",kind="written",pieces={"notebook"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Garden notes",body="I filled the barrel from the field line after the spray treatment. Those beans withered within days. The row watered from saved rainwater stayed green."},
{id="t0436-09",kind="written",pieces={"receipt"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Receipt",body="Three calves were off their feed in the pen that received the new grain. The others had the same weather and the same night watch but ate from an unopened older sack.\n\nI was supposed to balance the feed bill. Instead I drew the pen divisions on the back of the envelope."},
{id="t0436-10",kind="written",pieces={"letter"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="mailbox",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Letter",body="The lower garden took the muddy overflow from the field. The upper garden stayed dry. A week later the lower leaves had black edges and the upper cabbage was still growing.\n\nI meant to take a photograph for the seed supplier. The camera was full of birthday pictures and I could not bring myself to use the last frame."},
-- T0437
{id="t0437-01",kind="written",pieces={"receipt"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="vehicle",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Receipt",body="I counted three farms on the driver's usual loop. The first two took the pale sacks and each called about sick animals. The third refused the load because its storage room was full.\n\nHe was annoyed about bringing half his cargo home. I remember that because he made me sign for the return before he'd carry in my flour."},
{id="t0437-02",kind="written",pieces={"diary"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="vehicle",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Diary entry",body="I drove the field worker to town after his boots split. He had come from the treated rows that morning. He shivered in my car while my sister, who had worked the covered greenhouse, complained only about the heat.\n\nWe bought a cheap pair of boots and left the old ones wrapped in newspaper. I never finished paying her back for the fuel."},
{id="t0437-03",kind="written",pieces={"notepad"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="vehicle",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Notepad page",body="The first house took drinking water from a barrel beside the sprayed field. The next house had a covered well and said its children were eating normally.\n\nI carried the same groceries to both doors. The bread went stale at the first one because nobody wanted it."},
{id="t0437-04",kind="written",pieces={"letter"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="mailbox",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Letter",body="The truck carried bagged seed on Monday, then produce on Tuesday without washing the bed. Green dust was still in the corners where the produce crates sat.\n\nI helped unload and found the dust on my cuffs. It was easier to make a joke about the driver's housekeeping than to ask him to turn around."},
{id="t0437-05",kind="written",pieces={"notepad"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Notepad page",body="One stop on my route turned back the replacement feed because there was no room for it. That man's animals were still feeding when the others stopped drinking.\n\nHis wife told me not to treat this as good luck. I wrote the dates on a grocery list in case I forgot which week the truck had gone through."},
{id="t0437-06",kind="written",pieces={"diary"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Diary entry",body="I lent our shovel across the fence after we dug the sprayed ditch by the bean rows. Their field had not been sprayed. They returned it with the same pale clay on its blade, and their beans where the dog dug have since gone yellow and curled.\n\nI meant to scrub it before the children used it in the garden. It stayed by the door."},
{id="t0437-07",kind="written",pieces={"receipt"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Receipt",body="The boxes of greens came in with gritty water underneath. The dry boxes delivered an hour earlier stayed crisp; these left soft stems and the same green mark on my hands.\n\nI put them on separate shelves. The receipt printer was broken, so I wrote the difference on the back of my own shopping list."},
{id="t0437-08",kind="written",pieces={"letter"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="mailbox",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Letter",body="The second farm borrowed the trailer after the feed run. No one rinsed the corners. Two days later they called about the young goats, though their own feed had not changed.\n\nI had wanted to lend them a clean blanket too, but there was only room for the trailer and a sack of bedding."},
{id="t0437-09",kind="written",pieces={"notebook"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="vehicle",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Notebook page",body="Rain got through the canvas at the front of the load. The wet bags came apart; the dry bags at the back held their shape. The wet grain went out to the pens first.\n\nI put a mark on my pocket list so I'd remember which pen got which. It felt petty to count sacks while the animals refused breakfast."},
{id="t0437-10",kind="written",pieces={"receipt"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="vehicle",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Receipt",body="I took the field crew home in two trips. The crew who sprayed the south rows looked tired before sundown. The crew who repaired the fence away from those rows argued about pay all the way back.\n\nThey shared a truck and the same sandwiches. I wrote their tasks down on the back of a fuel receipt because the faces were beginning to blur."},
-- T0438
{id="t0438-01",kind="written",pieces={"diary"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Diary entry",body="We caught the same rain in two places. The barrel by the fields stood open; the cistern beneath the roof stayed shut. Only the barrel grew a green ring and left the dog unwilling to drink.\n\nI promised to paint the cistern lid when the weather cleared. It seems absurd now that I was worried about the color."},
{id="t0438-02",kind="written",pieces={"notepad"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Notepad page",body="Water from the low ditch left grit in our kitchen pail. The ditch runs along the sprayed oat field, and the well water was clear. My father drank the ditch water at work and spent the next morning unable to stand.\n\nI saved the grit in a little jar. The oats along the ditch have gone yellow in a strip."},
{id="t0438-03",kind="written",pieces={"letter"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="mailbox",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Letter",body="The sprayed field ran into the pond during the storm. The pond fish floated up the next morning, but the pond behind the hill still had them moving below the surface.\n\nMy nephew had planned to fish both ponds. I took away his net and told him we'd go when the water was clear."},
{id="t0438-04",kind="written",pieces={"notebook"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Notebook page",body="The gardener filled six watering cans from the field line, where the spray tank drains, and four from the house tap. Only the beds watered from the field line lost their new leaves.\n\nThe gardener says the cans were identical. I checked the roots because I wanted him to be wrong; they were brown and soft."},
{id="t0438-05",kind="written",pieces={"diary"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Diary entry",body="The greenhouse well was capped for repairs, so the workers used the open tank outside the trial rows. Three complained of a bitter taste before their afternoon break; the repair crew drank from a jug brought from home.\n\nI brought the jug myself. It stayed half full, and I kept wishing I had brought enough for everyone."},
{id="t0438-06",kind="written",pieces={"letter"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="mailbox",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Letter",body="A thin layer of pale dust settled on the downstream bank after the fields were washed. The upstream bank had only the usual silt. The chickens pecked at the lower bank and would not eat supper.\n\nI had gone down there to collect smooth stones for my daughter. I left the stones and came back for the birds."},
{id="t0438-07",kind="written",pieces={"diary"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Diary entry",body="I set out two dishes for the dog, one beneath the eaves and one beside the field gate. The gate dish gathered green specks overnight. The dog sniffed it and drank the covered one dry.\n\nThe gate dish was a wedding gift and I felt foolish testing rain in it. I washed it twice and the mark came back when it dried."},
{id="t0438-08",kind="written",pieces={"notepad"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Notepad page",body="The family by the lower road asked me to boil their water. A green ring stuck inside the kettle. My own well water boiled in it before without leaving a mark.\n\nTheir youngest carried the kettle to my door because his mother was too weak. I put it on the stove before he had finished speaking."},
{id="t0438-09",kind="written",pieces={"notebook"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Notebook page",body="The ditch by the seeded field held dead minnows in the shallows. The creek beyond the ridge still had live fish. My neighbor wanted to blame the heat, though both waters were under the same sun.\n\nWe had meant to take the children wading. I folded their towels away and kept the little sketch I made of the two channels."},
{id="t0438-10",kind="written",pieces={"notepad"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Notepad page",body="When the new field powder arrived, the water trough nearest the mixing shed developed a chalky edge. The closed reservoir at the far end did not. The animals pushed past one another to drink from the far one.\n\nI was asked to check the fences, so I did. I also wrote down where each trough was filled; that part was my own idea."},
-- T0439
{id="t0439-01",kind="written",pieces={"diary"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Diary entry",body="I fed the hens from the upper bin on Monday. They laid as usual. Tuesday's scoop came from the lower bin after the delivery, and by Thursday they had stopped laying.\n\nI cleaned the nesting boxes twice before I thought about which grain I had used. The lower bin still smells sweet when opened."},
{id="t0439-02",kind="written",pieces={"letter"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="mailbox",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Letter",body="Two dogs found the spilled feed by the unloading ramp. The neighbor's dog stayed tied at home and kept asking for scraps at supper. The two strays lay under the ramp by morning.\n\nI took bowls down to them because I thought they were hungry. Their water was untouched; the feed pile was smaller."},
{id="t0439-03",kind="written",pieces={"notepad"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Pasture notes",body="The sheep that pushed through grazed the sprayed trial plot. They went off their feed within the week. I kept the others on our grass and they stayed healthy."},
{id="t0439-04",kind="written",pieces={"diary"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Diary entry",body="The hens closest to the open feed sacks left thin shells. The birds behind the closed partition laid hard shells that cracked normally in my hands.\n\nI kept the eggs separate in two bowls. My daughter was annoyed because she thought I was sorting them by size for a cake."},
{id="t0439-05",kind="written",pieces={"receipt"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Receipt",body="A new sack reached the pigs before the horses. The pigs lost their appetite first; the horses were still eating the old grain from the blue barrel.\n\nI put the empty sack under a stone. I had paid for both loads and did not want a dispute over which delivery came first."},
{id="t0439-06",kind="written",pieces={"notebook"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Farm journal",body="The cows grazed near the ditch after they sprayed the upper field. Rain came that night and ran through. The high pasture cows kept feeding normal. I drew the gate closed so nobody would mix them."},
{id="t0439-07",kind="written",pieces={"notepad"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Notepad page",body="I sprouted two handfuls from different bags in jars by the same window. The older grain opened. The new grain made a film on the glass and did not grow.\n\nI wanted to prove the supplier had sent dead seed, which seemed an ordinary nuisance. The smell that followed was new to me."},
{id="t0439-08",kind="written",pieces={"diary"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Diary entry",body="The mill cat ate spilled grain from the fresh shipment and stopped hunting. The other cat slept upstairs where the old stores were, and still stole my lunch.\n\nI had scolded the first cat for leaving a mouse at my feet. The next day it did not come when I shook the tin."},
{id="t0439-09",kind="written",pieces={"letter"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="mailbox",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Letter",body="We filled one pan from the new bag and one from the sack left over from winter. The chickens chose both without hesitation. By evening the ones from the new pan stood still in the corner.\n\nMy father asked me to take away both pans. I kept the grain apart, though it meant washing another dish."},
{id="t0439-10",kind="written",pieces={"diary"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Diary entry",body="The ducks went into the field pond while the chickens stayed in the dry yard. By supper the ducks drifted at the bank. The chickens still fought over the scraps.\n\nI had never seen the ducks ignore bread. I left it where it fell and went inside for the net."},
-- T0440
{id="t0440-01",kind="written",pieces={"diary"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Diary entry",body="I worked the irrigation pump after the trial mix spilled near its intake. The handle left a pale smear on my hand. The other worker who stayed at the dry well never touched the pump and ate supper.\n\nMy palms began to itch before we heard about any illness in town. I had intended to borrow his gloves the following day."},
{id="t0440-02",kind="written",pieces={"letter"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="mailbox",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Letter",body="The feed truck dropped its first load at our farm. We swept the bed but the seam still held green grit when it collected another family's produce. They called two days later about a strange taste.\n\nI had swept that seam myself. I went back with a stiff brush and could still lift a pinch of the same grit."},
{id="t0440-03",kind="written",pieces={"notebook"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Notebook page",body="The truck driver tied the wet sacks on the outside of the load to dry. Seeds fell where the road crossed the creek, and the goats began to graze there.\n\nI found a torn strip of sack on the fence. My first thought was that somebody would expect me to pay for the lost grain."},
{id="t0440-04",kind="written",pieces={"notepad"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Notepad page",body="The crew washed their sprayers in the yard by the shared drain. The next morning our downspout bucket carried a green ring. The covered barrel beside the house did not.\n\nI used the bucket for mopping before I looked at the rim. The floor smelled like the field, so I took the mop outside."},
{id="t0440-05",kind="written",pieces={"diary"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Seed apron",body="My sister wore her seed treatment apron home and hung it on the line. Yellow-green dust fell from it onto the baby clothes below. I moved it to the porch when the dust left stains on my fingers."},
{id="t0440-06",kind="written",pieces={"letter"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="mailbox",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Letter",body="We raked the treated plot, then used the rake on the garden behind the house. The first garden row the rake touched curled at the tips; the last row, planted later with a clean tool, stayed straight.\n\nI knew whose rake it was because the handle had my initials burned into it. I had not noticed what lodged between the teeth."},
{id="t0440-07",kind="written",pieces={"receipt"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="vehicle",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Receipt",body="The first owner carried field bags in the trailer. The next carried hay to an untouched farm. Powder remained behind the hinges, and the animals fed from the hay before they showed any trouble.\n\nI wrote down who had the trailer on which day because we shared the hire fee. None of us was thinking about what had collected in the hinges."},
{id="t0440-08",kind="written",pieces={"diary"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Diary entry",body="I turned the field gloves inside out and carried them in my coat. The lining had dust from the mixing shed; my clean scarf picked it up before I got home.\n\nThe scarf was a gift. I nearly washed it with the rest of the laundry but could see where the dust had transferred."},
{id="t0440-09",kind="written",pieces={"notepad"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Notepad page",body="They borrowed our bucket to rinse a field tank. When it came back, the inside had a faint green line. My son used it to water the beans; only that bed browned along its edges.\n\nI should have checked it before lending it to him. He wanted to help and had already filled it when I saw the mark."},
{id="t0440-10",kind="written",pieces={"notebook"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Notebook page",body="The grain sacks stood beside the mill's intake fan. Pale treated-seed powder from their seams got into the flour bags nearest the fan, and those bags show a grey cast; the bags stacked behind the far wall remained white.\n\nThe miller said we could exchange the nearest bags. I wrote their positions down because all the labels looked the same."},
-- T0441
{id="t0441-01",kind="written",pieces={"diary"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Diary entry",body="We had two packets of the same seed. The packet kept sealed in the kitchen sprouted in a damp cloth. The open packet used beside the treated field did not; its kernels stained the cloth gray.\n\nI left both cloths on the windowsill. My mother kept asking when I would clear the mess away."},
{id="t0441-02",kind="written",pieces={"notebook"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Notebook page",body="The lower beds received the runoff from the new fields. The hill beds got the same rain but no runoff. Only the lower leaves curled and only the family tending them complained of a bitter taste at the tap.\n\nI marked the beds in my own sketch because I had promised to bring them seedlings. I still had healthy ones from the hill."},
{id="t0441-03",kind="written",pieces={"notepad"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Notepad page",body="We mixed half a sack from the new delivery with the old feed for one pen. Another pen stayed on the old feed alone. Both had the same keeper; only the mixed pen went quiet overnight.\n\nThe keeper was my uncle. He had insisted the new grain smelled better. I wrote down the scoops before we argued about memory."},
{id="t0441-04",kind="written",pieces={"letter"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="mailbox",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Letter",body="The trial crew stopped their work where the fence collapsed. Plants behind the broken fence stayed green; those along the completed rows carried small white spots the next day.\n\nI repaired the fence with my neighbor. We left the corner open on purpose once we saw how different the rows looked."},
{id="t0441-05",kind="written",pieces={"receipt"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Receipt",body="The crates under canvas went to one shop; the uncovered crates from the same field went to another. The uncovered leaves had a fine gritty edge and spoiled first.\n\nI bought a bunch from each shop so I could compare them in my kitchen. The shopkeepers both thought I was bargaining over pennies."},
{id="t0441-06",kind="written",pieces={"diary"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Diary entry",body="Nothing fell from the sky for six days. The upper field stayed sound while the trial plot wilted after its second application. The nearest laborers started missing meals before the rain came.\n\nI had written the dry days down because I hoped they would end. Now I keep turning back to that part of the calendar."},
{id="t0441-07",kind="written",pieces={"notepad"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Notepad page",body="Both gardens shared a well. Only the beds beside the treated field received drifting dust; the wall sheltered the others. The exposed beans yellowed first.\n\nI thought the wall was stealing light from the sheltered beans. They grew taller anyway. My sister wanted to pull them up for supper."},
{id="t0441-08",kind="written",pieces={"diary"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Diary entry",body="Birds kept pecking at the old grain spilled by the shed. They avoided the new spill from the sacks, even when the old pile was nearly gone.\n\nI swept neither pile because I wanted to see if they would change their minds. The owner complained that I was leaving a mess beside his door."},
{id="t0441-09",kind="written",pieces={"letter"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="mailbox",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Letter",body="Both baskets held vegetables from the same planting. One came from the sprayed edge and softened by morning; the other, picked beyond the ditch, stayed crisp.\n\nI marked the handles with string. They were borrowed baskets and I knew I would have to return them even if I could no longer sell what was inside."},
{id="t0441-10",kind="written",pieces={"notebook"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Notebook page",body="The near trough was topped up from the runoff ditch of the sprayed pasture and the far trough from a tank. The animals walked past the near trough without drinking; the grass at the ditch edge is scorched and the hose still smells of spray.\n\nI made a sketch of the pipe before anyone moved the hose."},
}}
